{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AmoSBDkTk5kPjkhTE7JtkU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_personfit_contam\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (用户确认；ARR submission DDL 5/25 — 需确认可行性)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (abstract 7/21, full paper 7/28, ~10 weeks)\n6\t- Backup: ICLR 2027 (~Sep 2026, ~17 weeks)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n9\t\n10\t**Claim 1 (Minimal-Information Detection Framework + Controlled Validation)**:\n11\tIRT person-fit statistics provide a principled contamination detection framework at the minimal-information operating point — requiring only binary response patterns. Simulation establishes high theoretical detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks), and bootstrap null distributions are well-calibrated for large benchmarks (MMLU/HellaSwag KS reject 8.3%, but overall 40% due to small benchmarks like HumanEval 75%, ARC-C 58.3% — calibration degrades with n_items). In simulation, lz* matches or outperforms supervised binary classifiers (LR/RF with oracle labels) at low contamination (5-10%), leveraging IRT structure as inductive bias. Controlled contamination experiments (QLoRA SFT injection on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct) validate the framework across model families: Qwen at 15% contamination yields |Cohen's d|=3.42 (n=3, ddof=1, ℓz*-corrected) with clear seen/unseen memorization fingerprint; Llama confirms cross-family detection with |Cohen's d|=2.95 at 15% and 3.31 at 50% (n=3, ddof=1, ℓz*-corrected), both large effects. θ-fixed analysis reveals a θ-shift boundary condition: when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data, detection sensitivity can degrade (model-dependent; Qwen shows free-θ non-monotonicity due to high baseline misfit, Llama does not), but fixing θ to pre-contamination baseline restores monotonic dose-response in both families. The memorization fraction (~35-38% at 15% contamination, consistent across families) quantifies the SFT generalization effect.\n12\t\n13\t**Claim 2 (Detection Characterization)**:\n14\tDetection power increases with benchmark size (n_items) and varies with contamination level, following an empirical power function (R²=0.65) that provides approximate practical guidance for practitioners assessing detectability on benchmarks of known size — but should NOT be described as \"predictive theory\" or \"scaling law.\" Two distinct signal regimes: partial contamination produces aberrant patterns (lz* << 0), full contamination produces over-consistent patterns (lz* >> 0). For sufficiently large benchmarks (≥10K items), theoretical power exceeds 90% at 15% contamination. Note: power function gives an **upper bound** (assumes all contaminated items produce aberrant signal); SFT generalization reduces effective signal — ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction to derive adjusted (\"expected\") power. Both upper bound and adjusted power should be reported. **Baseline comparison (exp-baseline-comparison)**: At model level, lz* achieves 8× the effect size of classical person-fit statistics (Guttman/U3) on identical data (|d|=3.42 vs |d|=0.43 for Qwen 15%), demonstrating the value of full 4PL IRT parameterization. At item level, ALL binary-only methods achieve near-random discrimination (AUROC 0.52–0.63, including oracle supervised classifiers), revealing contamination produces a diffuse statistical signature detectable only through model-level aggregation over thousands of items. Accuracy z-score trivially detects in controlled settings (z=160 due to near-zero accuracy variance) but lacks specificity in real-world scenarios. The IRT framework enables principled aggregation by calibrating each item's expected response probability.\n15\t\n16\t**Claim 3 (Empirical Findings from Real LLM Data)**:\n17\tThree empirical findings from applying IRT person-fit to real LLM response data: (a) **Universal 4PL model misfit** — nearly all (model, benchmark) cells produce extreme lz* values (|lz*| >> 5, 57/60 cells flagged after BH-FDR correction), revealing that LLM response patterns fundamentally differ from classical test-taker patterns. This is a genuine property of LLM responses (bootstrap null is well-calibrated), not a statistical artifact. The simulation-to-reality gap motivates the Δlz* design. (b) **PSN-IRT 12-model case study** — detailed anomaly profiles with validated 4PL parameters (Gemini-1.5: 100% MMLU accuracy, lz*=+31.81, θ=0.78; selective vs uniform misfit patterns across benchmarks; Ward clustering reveals contamination typology). (c) **IRT parameter estimation challenges** — MML-EM refit from v1 leaderboard data (N=63→178, covering all available models) yields b_r=0.66 (partial difficulty validation) but a_r≈0.13 (discrimination failure, well below 0.2 threshold), quantifying the sample size gap between classical IRT and neural IRT estimation in LLM contexts. 13K+ model per-item data is publicly available for future large-scale audits once estimation challenges are resolved.\n18\t\n19\t## Story Spine\n20\t\n21\t**Problem**: Benchmark contamination undermines LLM evaluation reliability. As benchmarks proliferate and training corpora grow, contamination risk increases, but all existing detection methods require privileged access — training data (n-gram overlap), token probabilities (Min-K%, MIA), model weights (internal probing), or specially crafted prompts (Time Travel). A contaminated LLM is functionally analogous to an examinee with item preknowledge, yet no work has connected the mature psychometric literature on cheating detection to LLM benchmark integrity.\n22\t\n23\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods circa 2026 span five families: time-based partition, MIA/Min-K%++ (ICLR 2024), Time Travel probing (ICLR 2024 Spotlight), ConStat performance-based testing (NeurIPS 2024), and CoDeC in-context learning effects (ICLR 2026). Wang et al. (2025) show all MIA-based methods fail under post-RL contamination. Critically, ALL require more than binary response patterns — no method operates at the minimal-information level.\n24\t\n25\t**Our framing**: We establish the minimal-information operating point on the contamination detection frontier. By repurposing IRT person-fit statistics — developed over decades for detecting exam cheating — we ask: \"What can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" We show: (1) in simulation, person-fit statistics achieve high detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks) with well-calibrated null distributions; (2) in real LLM data, response patterns universally deviate from 4PL predictions — the statistical framework is sound, but LLMs genuinely violate IRT assumptions (local independence, unidimensionality), producing extreme lz* values across nearly all models; (3) controlled contamination experiments leverage this by measuring Δlz* between clean and contaminated models — since the null is well-calibrated, within-model shifts are statistically interpretable. The universal model misfit finding is itself a contribution — it reveals that LLM response patterns are fundamentally different from classical test-taker patterns.\n26\t\n27\t**Headline result template**: \"Using only binary response patterns from the target model (with externally calibrated IRT item parameters), IRT-FIT detects controlled contamination with |Cohen's d|>2.9 across two model families (Qwen, Llama), achieving 8× the effect size of classical person-fit statistics (Guttman/U3). The HT statistic (requiring only item difficulty) achieves comparable model-level detection power — the IRT person-fit family collectively dominates simpler indices, with ℓz*'s advantage lying in mechanistic interpretability (θ-shift analysis, memorization fraction quantification) and [pending: post-RL robustness vs HT]. Model-level aggregation over thousands of items yields robust detection where all item-level methods are near-random (AUROC 0.52–0.63). The IRT framework provides unique mechanistic insight: θ-shift analysis reveals how contamination raises ability estimates, and memorization fraction (35–38%) bridges theoretical power (97.9%) and observed detection capacity.\"\n28\t\n29\t## Venue Fit Risks\n30\t\n31\t- **EMNLP**: NLP evaluation methodology fits well. Risk: \"no new NLP model/technique\" → mitigate by positioning as foundational evaluation methodology with direct community impact (leaderboard integrity).\n32\t- **AAAI**: PSN-IRT was AAAI 2026 Oral — strong psychometrics+AI audience. Risk: less NLP-specific reviewer pool.\n33\t- **Cross-discipline concern**: IRT/psychometrics may be unfamiliar to ML reviewers → need self-contained exposition in Section 3 (IRT background), avoid jargon, provide intuitive explanations.\n34\t\n35\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n36\t\n37\t| # | Concern | Response Strategy | Supporting Experiment |\n38\t|---|---------|------------------|----------------------|\n39\t| R1 | \"Just applying existing IRT to LLMs\" | Frame as establishing new operating point, not cross-domain transfer. Person-fit for contamination is unexplored. Downgrade \"cross-domain\" from contribution to background. | — |\n40\t| R2 | \"No ground truth contamination labels\" | Controlled contamination experiment (fine-tune clean models on benchmark items). Phase B anomalies are converging evidence, not proof. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n41\t| R3 | \"Power too low for small benchmarks\" | Present power function analysis as contribution, not limitation. Derive theoretical relationship. | exp-power-theory |\n42\t| R4 | \"Only 12 models\" | 12 models with validated 4PL parameters provide detailed anomaly profiles. Universal misfit (57/60 flagged) spans sufficient models to establish the pattern. 13K+ v1 per-item data availability discussed as future work. Ctrl-contam covers 4-5 model families. | exp-ctrl-contam, phase_b_personfit |\n43\t| R5 | \"SFT generalization smooths signal\" | Controlled experiment includes domain-level analysis. Discuss hard-item contamination resistance. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n44\t| R6 | \"Absolute lz* thresholds don't work on real data\" | Bootstrap null is well-calibrated (KS pass for large benchmarks); the issue is LLMs genuinely deviate from 4PL. Universal model misfit is a finding, not an artifact. Δlz* leverages the well-calibrated null for within-model comparisons. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-empirical-null |\n45\t| R7 | \"Post-RL contamination?\" | Hypothesis test: GRPO after SFT contamination on Qwen 3.5-9B. | exp-post-rl |\n46\t| R8 | \"4PL vs 3PL — does d parameter matter?\" | Ablation comparing 4PL vs 3PL(d=1) detection sensitivity. | exp-4pl-ablation |\n47\t| R9 | \"No same-level binary-only baselines\" | **Completed (exp-baseline-comparison)**: Model-level: lz* |d|=3.42 vs Guttman/U3 |d|=0.43 (8× gap) — full IRT parameterization far exceeds difficulty-only person-fit. **HT is nearly as powerful as ℓz* (avg |d| comparable)** — the \"8×\" headline must include HT comparison to avoid selective framing. Item-level: all methods near-random (AUROC 0.52–0.63). acc z-score detects trivially (z=160) but lacks specificity. | exp-baseline-comparison |\n48\t| R12 | \"HT ≈ ℓz* — why use ℓz*?\" | **[Dream D2 三档一致]** HT achieves comparable |d| with weaker requirements (difficulty only, no 4PL). **四场景应对 (D022, Reviewer validated)**：(Best) HT post-RL 丢失 + ℓz* 保留 → headline 差异化；(Good) HT 弱化 + ℓz* 更强 → quantitative comparison；(Neutral) 均保留 → 转用数据无关差异化（见下）；(Bad) 均丢失 → negative-as-contribution, scope SFT。**数据无关差异化（任何场景均可用）**：(i) ℓz* 有参数化 null (≈N(0,1), bootstrap 已验证) → 可直接假设检验, HT 无此性质；(ii) Snijders 校正补偿 θ 估计误差 (Var*=Var_l - C²/I(θ)), HT 无此校正；(iii) ℓz* 用 a/b/c/d 四参数加权 item 贡献, HT 仅用 b → MMLU 跨 57 科目 item 异质性大时 ℓz* 理论更精确。这些点不依赖 post-RL 结果，论文中应明确讨论。 | exp-baseline-comparison, exp-post-rl |\n49\t| R13 | \"Minimal-information overstates\" | **[Dream D2 三档一致]** \"Minimal-information operating point\" obscures PSN-IRT 4PL parameter dependency. Reframe to \"minimal information **from the target model**\" or \"minimal runtime information\" — explicitly acknowledge PSN-IRT calibration as an external input requirement. | — |\n50\t| R10 | \"Leaderboard audit baseline unreliable\" | Leaderboard audit abandoned (D011). ctrl-contam is the validated detection. 12-model case study uses PSN-IRT validated parameters directly (no baseline estimation needed). v1 data availability noted as future work. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n51\t| R11 | \"Power function is upper bound\" | Report both theoretical upper bound AND adjusted power (memorization fraction from ctrl-contam seen/unseen split). Gap = SFT generalization effect quantification. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-power-theory |\n52\t\n53\t## Key Narrative Elements (from External Review + Distillation)\n54\t\n55\t1. **Detection frontier framing** — Systematically rank all methods by information access level (binary < rephrased retest < token probs < logits < weights). IRT-FIT defines the bottom of this frontier.\n56\t2. **Definitional pivot (à la ConStat)** — \"All prior contamination detection methods require privileged access. We ask a more fundamental question: what can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" This reframes our work as problem reformulation, not just cross-domain transfer.\n57\t3. **RL-robustness as structural advantage** — Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) proves all 10 log-prob methods ≈ random on RL-trained reasoning models. Person-fit operates on binary response patterns, not token distributions — structurally immune to RL-induced distributional shifts. This is our strongest motivation against log-prob baselines.\n58\t4. **Scalability potential (deferred to future work)** — 13K+ v1 per-item data publicly available. IRT-FIT is uniquely suited for retrospective audit (only needs archival binary data). BUT: current paper does NOT include large-scale audit (D011: IRT refit failed). Mention data availability + roadmap in Discussion/Future Work. NEVER claim \"leaderboard audit\" or \"large-scale detection\" in current paper.\n59\t5. **Inverted-U as empirical characterization** — Derive from: (a) contamination→0%: signal drowned in sampling noise; (b) contamination→100%: identifiability collapse. Simulation fit R²=0.957; real-data fit R²=0.65 (gap due to SFT generalization). Frame as \"empirical trend\" not \"theory/law.\"\n60\t6. **Baseline comparison as evidence for model-level aggregation** — Item-level detection is near-random for ALL binary-only methods (including oracle RF). This is NOT a weakness — it reveals that contamination signal is diffuse (memorization fraction ~35%). Model-level lz* aggregates 14K weak signals into |d|>2.9. Frame item-level weakness as supporting evidence: \"any method that aggregates is better than any method that localizes.\" lz* vs Guttman/U3 8× gap proves IRT parameterization matters. acc z-score is sensitive but non-specific (sensitivity-specificity tradeoff).\n61\t7. **Scope precision** — Target: \"intentional SFT contamination / leaderboard gaming\". Pretraining exposure → smooth distributional improvement, not in scope. Honest scoping > vague claims.\n62\t8. **Terminology guard** — NEVER use \"binary information bottleneck\" or \"information-theoretic lower bound for all binary-only methods.\" We can only claim lz* (a specific statistic) has limitations under SFT generalization — NOT that all binary-only methods fail. Correct framing: \"IRT person-fit as a principled framework at the minimal-information operating point.\"\n63\t9. **Memorization fraction cross-family consistency** — MF is 35–38% at 15% contamination across Qwen (0.38) and Llama (0.35), only 3pp difference. Consistency strengthens generalizability. MF may vary with contamination mechanism (full FT vs QLoRA), model capacity, and benchmark difficulty — acknowledge in Limitations as deployment bootstrapping problem.\n64\t10. **Validation hierarchy** — ctrl-contam = primary validation (ground truth, same model clean vs contaminated); 12-model case study = empirical findings (no ground truth, but validated parameters); v1 data = future work roadmap. Paper structure should reflect this priority.\n65\t9. **lz* measures memorization, not generalization** — lz* detects aberrant patterns (memorization signature), not smooth ability improvement (generalization). This is a feature: it distinguishes genuine learning from rote memorization. Power function gives upper bound; ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction.\n66\t10. **Negative results as contributions** — D007 (universal misfit) and D008 (empirical null well-calibrated) are \"honest negative results that become positive contributions\": universal misfit is a novel finding about LLM response patterns; the simulation-reality gap motivates Δlz* and quantifies SFT generalization. D011 (MML-EM refit failure) is a methodological caveat (classical vs neural IRT sample requirements). D009 (item alignment) is a data engineering detail (1 sentence in Data section). Present negatives with the framing: \"the gap between where IRT works perfectly (simulation) and where it struggles (real LLM data) is itself informative.\"\n67\t11. **ctrl-contam actual results (D015)** — contam_15 |d|=3.85 (strong), contam_50 non-monotonic under free-θ but **monotonic under θ-fixed** (ratio=2.93). θ-shift is the mechanism: contamination→higher θ_MLE→absorbs aberrance signal. Frame as \"principled detection with quantified operating characteristics + θ-shift boundary condition.\" Headline: \"We don't just detect — we characterize, including the conditions under which detection degrades.\" Do NOT claim \"state-of-the-art detection.\"\n68\t12. **θ-shift as methodological contribution (D015)** — Person-fit sensitivity degrades when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data. This is a novel finding for contamination detection: (a) θ-fixed analysis recovers monotonic dose-response, (b) the θ-shift magnitude (0.47 at 50% contamination) quantifies the confound, (c) practical implication: use pre-contamination θ baseline or cross-validated θ. Present as a contribution, not a limitation.\n69\t13. **Cross-family baseline lz* divergence (Reviewer WARNING)** — Clean lz* spans ~9σ: Qwen +8.68, Mistral +5.42, Llama -0.14. 固定阈值检测失效（Qwen contam_15 lz*=+3.85 仍为正值）。论文必须：(a) 明确 IRT-FIT 是相对检测（Δlz*/Cohen's d），非绝对阈值；(b) 展示 clean baseline lz* 跨家族差异表；(c) 预防性回答\"contam_15 lz*=+3.85 为正值为何算污染\"（因为 Δlz*=-4.83 是大效应）；(d) lz* baseline 作为\"模型内部一致性\"指标——Mistral acc 最低(0.514)但 lz* 第二高(+5.42)，说明 lz* 捕捉 difficulty-ordering 一致性而非准确率。\n70\t14. **Inverted-U 是模型相关的** — Qwen 在 15%→50% 区间出现强 inversion（Δlz* 50%=-1.39 << 15%=-4.83），Llama 和 Mistral 在此区间 Δlz* 单调增大。Inverted-U 在 free-θ 下由 baseline misfit 调制——高 baseline lz* (Qwen +8.68) 的模型更容易出现 non-monotonicity。论文不能 claim inverted-U 为 universal phenomenon，需加 model-dependent caveat。θ-fixed 分析仍恢复所有家族的 monotonicity — 这是 θ-fixed 贡献的关键证据。\n71\t15. **seen/unseen split as strongest signal** — contam_15 seen lz*≈0 (memorized items look \"normal\") vs unseen lz*=3.1. This is the clearest contamination fingerprint: items that should produce aberrant responses instead produce expected responses. More interpretable than aggregate Δlz*.\n72\t\n73\t## Writing Strategy (from Distillation)\n74\t\n75\t- **Story type**: \"跨界迁移型\" — unused in 0/8 peer papers. Our unique angle.\n76\t- **Figure 1**: Problem illustration (dual-panel: contaminated vs clean response pattern). Use psychometric hook — impossible response pattern (hard items right, easy wrong).\n77\t- **Contribution structure**: 3 contributions (method + characterization + empirical findings), escalating scope. Standard in 5/8 papers.\n78\t- **Result tables**: Row=methods, col=datasets×metrics. Bold-best. Average column.\n79\t- **Numbered findings**: Adopt PSN-IRT's \"Key Discoveries\" strategy for scannable presentation.\n80\t- **CIs as differentiator**: 6/8 peer papers report no variance. Our bootstrap CIs are a competitive advantage.\n81\t- **Baseline count**: Peer median ~5. Target ≥5 baselines.\n82\t\n83\t## Evidence Summary\n84\t\n85\t- **Phase A (simulation)**: Null check passed (4PL compatible with lz* theory). MMLU power@15%=97.9%. Power ∝ n_items confirmed. Simulation results stand — they establish theoretical detection capacity within the 4PL model.\n86\t- **Phase B (real data)**: Gemini-1.5 MMLU acc=1.000, θ=0.78, lz*=+31.81. Cross-benchmark anomaly profiles identified.\n87\t- **Empirical null analysis (exp-empirical-null)**: Bootstrap null calibration is benchmark-size dependent — large benchmarks well-calibrated (MMLU: mean bias 0.041, std 1.003, KS reject 8.3%; HellaSwag: 8.3%), small benchmarks poorly calibrated (HumanEval: 75%, ARC-C: 58.3%; overall KS reject 40%, 24/60). The statistical framework is sound for large benchmarks (n>10K). 57/60 real-data cells flagged because LLM lz* values are genuinely extreme (|lz*| >> 5) — this reflects **universal 4PL model misfit** (LLM response patterns violate IRT assumptions), not contamination-specific detection. **Important**: 57/60 vs accuracy z-score 4/60 demonstrates lz* captures response-pattern information beyond aggregate accuracy (evidence for Claim 3a universal misfit), NOT contamination detection superiority. Contamination detection evidence comes from simulation (lz* AUROC 0.675 vs ML 0.575 at 5%) and ctrl-contam (d=3.42, n=3, ddof=1, ℓz*-corrected).\n88\t- **Calibration gap reframed (D007→D008)**: The gap is not \"null is biased\" but \"real LLM data genuinely deviates from 4PL\". This strengthens Δlz* approach: well-calibrated null means within-model shifts are statistically meaningful.\n89\t- **Controlled contamination (exp-ctrl-contam-pilot, D015, ℓz*-corrected)**: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct × MMLU, 4 conditions (0%×3 seeds, 15%, 50%). **n=3 clean seeds (ℓz*-corrected)**: s1=9.47, s2=7.05, s3=9.53 (s2 outlier; mean=8.68, std=1.41). Key results: (a) contam_15 |Cohen's d|=3.42 (n=3, ddof=1, strong effect); (b) contam_50 |d|=0.99 (n=3, ddof=1, borderline large); (c) free-θ dose-response non-monotonic and more extreme after correction (contam_50 Δlz*=1.40 < contam_15 Δlz*=4.84, ratio=3.46) due to θ-shift confound; (d) **θ-fixed analysis (ℓz*-corrected)**: θ_fixed=-0.0965 (n=3 clean θ_MLE mean, unchanged by ℓz* correction); lz*_fixed: contam_15=11.852, contam_50=18.576; Δlz*_fixed: contam_15=+3.17, contam_50=+9.89; ratio=3.12 (virtually unchanged from uncorrected 3.12 — Snijders correction scales proportionally); (e) seen/unseen memorization fingerprint; (f) memorization_fraction=0.38 (15%) and 0.29 (50%). θ-shift mechanism: contamination raises θ_MLE, absorbing aberrance signal — this is a methodological contribution. **Note**: all values ℓz*-corrected (Snijders 2001); prior uncorrected ℓz values archived as *_lz_uncorrected.json.\n90\t- **Cross-family validation (exp-ctrl-contam-llama, ℓz*-corrected)**: Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct × MMLU, 3+2 conditions. **n=3 clean seeds (ℓz*-corrected)**: s1=0.845, s2=-0.182, s3=-1.084 (mean=-0.14, std=0.97). contam_15 lz*=-2.992 (θ=-0.276), contam_50 lz*=-3.331 (θ=-0.149). Δlz*: contam_15=-3.84, contam_50=-4.18, both significant. **Cohen's d (n=3, ddof=1)**: contam_15 d=-2.95 (large), contam_50 d=-3.31 (large), monotonic (|d_50|>|d_15|) — contrasting Qwen's non-monotonicity. **Free-θ**: slight monotonicity (ratio=1.09), contrasting Qwen's strong non-monotonicity (ratio=3.46). **θ_fixed (θ=-0.666)**: lz*_fixed contam_15=0.959, contam_50=1.172; Δlz*_fixed=+0.114/+0.327; ratio=2.87 (enhances monotonicity). θ-shift mechanism universal: Δθ Llama 0.39/0.52, Qwen 0.29/0.47. Memorization fraction ~0.33-0.38. **Narrative**: Qwen story = \"θ_fixed repairs non-monotonicity\"; Llama story = \"θ_fixed enhances existing monotonicity\". Both confirm θ_fixed recovers/strengthens dose-response. Non-monotonicity is model-dependent (modulated by baseline misfit magnitude). Qwen clean lz*=8.68 vs Llama -0.14 — discuss in §6. **Cross-family Cohen's d summary**: Qwen d_15=-3.42/d_50=-0.99; Llama d_15=-2.95/d_50=-3.31. Both families |d|>2.9 at 15%, confirming detection generalizes.\n91\t- **4PL real-data degradation**: 3PL(d=1) vs 4PL lz* correlation r=0.225, RMSE=68.41. d parameter essential for high-ability models (DeepSeek-V3 Δ=357). Complements simulation ablation (+14-27pp power gain).\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea1e9cd0-76ef-4277-8837-49ffa06069a9","uuid":"f8e4f1b4-4f15-4aa9-849b-bd2e6bac55a6","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:55:59.011Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122444/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_personfit_contam\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (用户确认；ARR submission DDL 5/25 — 需确认可行性)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (abstract 7/21, full paper 7/28, ~10 weeks)\n- Backup: ICLR 2027 (~Sep 2026, ~17 weeks)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n**Claim 1 (Minimal-Information Detection Framework + Controlled Validation)**:\nIRT person-fit statistics provide a principled contamination detection framework at the minimal-information operating point — requiring only binary response patterns. Simulation establishes high theoretical detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks), and bootstrap null distributions are well-calibrated for large benchmarks (MMLU/HellaSwag KS reject 8.3%, but overall 40% due to small benchmarks like HumanEval 75%, ARC-C 58.3% — calibration degrades with n_items). In simulation, lz* matches or outperforms supervised binary classifiers (LR/RF with oracle labels) at low contamination (5-10%), leveraging IRT structure as inductive bias. Controlled contamination experiments (QLoRA SFT injection on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct) validate the framework across model families: Qwen at 15% contamination yields |Cohen's d|=3.42 (n=3, ddof=1, ℓz*-corrected) with clear seen/unseen memorization fingerprint; Llama confirms cross-family detection with |Cohen's d|=2.95 at 15% and 3.31 at 50% (n=3, ddof=1, ℓz*-corrected), both large effects. θ-fixed analysis reveals a θ-shift boundary condition: when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data, detection sensitivity can degrade (model-dependent; Qwen shows free-θ non-monotonicity due to high baseline misfit, Llama does not), but fixing θ to pre-contamination baseline restores monotonic dose-response in both families. The memorization fraction (~35-38% at 15% contamination, consistent across families) quantifies the SFT generalization effect.\n\n**Claim 2 (Detection Characterization)**:\nDetection power increases with benchmark size (n_items) and varies with contamination level, following an empirical power function (R²=0.65) that provides approximate practical guidance for practitioners assessing detectability on benchmarks of known size — but should NOT be described as \"predictive theory\" or \"scaling law.\" Two distinct signal regimes: partial contamination produces aberrant patterns (lz* << 0), full contamination produces over-consistent patterns (lz* >> 0). For sufficiently large benchmarks (≥10K items), theoretical power exceeds 90% at 15% contamination. Note: power function gives an **upper bound** (assumes all contaminated items produce aberrant signal); SFT generalization reduces effective signal — ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction to derive adjusted (\"expected\") power. Both upper bound and adjusted power should be reported. **Baseline comparison (exp-baseline-comparison)**: At model level, lz* achieves 8× the effect size of classical person-fit statistics (Guttman/U3) on identical data (|d|=3.42 vs |d|=0.43 for Qwen 15%), demonstrating the value of full 4PL IRT parameterization. At item level, ALL binary-only methods achieve near-random discrimination (AUROC 0.52–0.63, including oracle supervised classifiers), revealing contamination produces a diffuse statistical signature detectable only through model-level aggregation over thousands of items. Accuracy z-score trivially detects in controlled settings (z=160 due to near-zero accuracy variance) but lacks specificity in real-world scenarios. The IRT framework enables principled aggregation by calibrating each item's expected response probability.\n\n**Claim 3 (Empirical Findings from Real LLM Data)**:\nThree empirical findings from applying IRT person-fit to real LLM response data: (a) **Universal 4PL model misfit** — nearly all (model, benchmark) cells produce extreme lz* values (|lz*| >> 5, 57/60 cells flagged after BH-FDR correction), revealing that LLM response patterns fundamentally differ from classical test-taker patterns. This is a genuine property of LLM responses (bootstrap null is well-calibrated), not a statistical artifact. The simulation-to-reality gap motivates the Δlz* design. (b) **PSN-IRT 12-model case study** — detailed anomaly profiles with validated 4PL parameters (Gemini-1.5: 100% MMLU accuracy, lz*=+31.81, θ=0.78; selective vs uniform misfit patterns across benchmarks; Ward clustering reveals contamination typology). (c) **IRT parameter estimation challenges** — MML-EM refit from v1 leaderboard data (N=63→178, covering all available models) yields b_r=0.66 (partial difficulty validation) but a_r≈0.13 (discrimination failure, well below 0.2 threshold), quantifying the sample size gap between classical IRT and neural IRT estimation in LLM contexts. 13K+ model per-item data is publicly available for future large-scale audits once estimation challenges are resolved.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: Benchmark contamination undermines LLM evaluation reliability. As benchmarks proliferate and training corpora grow, contamination risk increases, but all existing detection methods require privileged access — training data (n-gram overlap), token probabilities (Min-K%, MIA), model weights (internal probing), or specially crafted prompts (Time Travel). A contaminated LLM is functionally analogous to an examinee with item preknowledge, yet no work has connected the mature psychometric literature on cheating detection to LLM benchmark integrity.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods circa 2026 span five families: time-based partition, MIA/Min-K%++ (ICLR 2024), Time Travel probing (ICLR 2024 Spotlight), ConStat performance-based testing (NeurIPS 2024), and CoDeC in-context learning effects (ICLR 2026). Wang et al. (2025) show all MIA-based methods fail under post-RL contamination. Critically, ALL require more than binary response patterns — no method operates at the minimal-information level.\n\n**Our framing**: We establish the minimal-information operating point on the contamination detection frontier. By repurposing IRT person-fit statistics — developed over decades for detecting exam cheating — we ask: \"What can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" We show: (1) in simulation, person-fit statistics achieve high detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks) with well-calibrated null distributions; (2) in real LLM data, response patterns universally deviate from 4PL predictions — the statistical framework is sound, but LLMs genuinely violate IRT assumptions (local independence, unidimensionality), producing extreme lz* values across nearly all models; (3) controlled contamination experiments leverage this by measuring Δlz* between clean and contaminated models — since the null is well-calibrated, within-model shifts are statistically interpretable. The universal model misfit finding is itself a contribution — it reveals that LLM response patterns are fundamentally different from classical test-taker patterns.\n\n**Headline result template**: \"Using only binary response patterns from the target model (with externally calibrated IRT item parameters), IRT-FIT detects controlled contamination with |Cohen's d|>2.9 across two model families (Qwen, Llama), achieving 8× the effect size of classical person-fit statistics (Guttman/U3). The HT statistic (requiring only item difficulty) achieves comparable model-level detection power — the IRT person-fit family collectively dominates simpler indices, with ℓz*'s advantage lying in mechanistic interpretability (θ-shift analysis, memorization fraction quantification) and [pending: post-RL robustness vs HT]. Model-level aggregation over thousands of items yields robust detection where all item-level methods are near-random (AUROC 0.52–0.63). The IRT framework provides unique mechanistic insight: θ-shift analysis reveals how contamination raises ability estimates, and memorization fraction (35–38%) bridges theoretical power (97.9%) and observed detection capacity.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **EMNLP**: NLP evaluation methodology fits well. Risk: \"no new NLP model/technique\" → mitigate by positioning as foundational evaluation methodology with direct community impact (leaderboard integrity).\n- **AAAI**: PSN-IRT was AAAI 2026 Oral — strong psychometrics+AI audience. Risk: less NLP-specific reviewer pool.\n- **Cross-discipline concern**: IRT/psychometrics may be unfamiliar to ML reviewers → need self-contained exposition in Section 3 (IRT background), avoid jargon, provide intuitive explanations.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n\n| # | Concern | Response Strategy | Supporting Experiment |\n|---|---------|------------------|----------------------|\n| R1 | \"Just applying existing IRT to LLMs\" | Frame as establishing new operating point, not cross-domain transfer. Person-fit for contamination is unexplored. Downgrade \"cross-domain\" from contribution to background. | — |\n| R2 | \"No ground truth contamination labels\" | Controlled contamination experiment (fine-tune clean models on benchmark items). Phase B anomalies are converging evidence, not proof. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R3 | \"Power too low for small benchmarks\" | Present power function analysis as contribution, not limitation. Derive theoretical relationship. | exp-power-theory |\n| R4 | \"Only 12 models\" | 12 models with validated 4PL parameters provide detailed anomaly profiles. Universal misfit (57/60 flagged) spans sufficient models to establish the pattern. 13K+ v1 per-item data availability discussed as future work. Ctrl-contam covers 4-5 model families. | exp-ctrl-contam, phase_b_personfit |\n| R5 | \"SFT generalization smooths signal\" | Controlled experiment includes domain-level analysis. Discuss hard-item contamination resistance. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R6 | \"Absolute lz* thresholds don't work on real data\" | Bootstrap null is well-calibrated (KS pass for large benchmarks); the issue is LLMs genuinely deviate from 4PL. Universal model misfit is a finding, not an artifact. Δlz* leverages the well-calibrated null for within-model comparisons. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-empirical-null |\n| R7 | \"Post-RL contamination?\" | Hypothesis test: GRPO after SFT contamination on Qwen 3.5-9B. | exp-post-rl |\n| R8 | \"4PL vs 3PL — does d parameter matter?\" | Ablation comparing 4PL vs 3PL(d=1) detection sensitivity. | exp-4pl-ablation |\n| R9 | \"No same-level binary-only baselines\" | **Completed (exp-baseline-comparison)**: Model-level: lz* |d|=3.42 vs Guttman/U3 |d|=0.43 (8× gap) — full IRT parameterization far exceeds difficulty-only person-fit. **HT is nearly as powerful as ℓz* (avg |d| comparable)** — the \"8×\" headline must include HT comparison to avoid selective framing. Item-level: all methods near-random (AUROC 0.52–0.63). acc z-score detects trivially (z=160) but lacks specificity. | exp-baseline-comparison |\n| R12 | \"HT ≈ ℓz* — why use ℓz*?\" | **[Dream D2 三档一致]** HT achieves comparable |d| with weaker requirements (difficulty only, no 4PL). **四场景应对 (D022, Reviewer validated)**：(Best) HT post-RL 丢失 + ℓz* 保留 → headline 差异化；(Good) HT 弱化 + ℓz* 更强 → quantitative comparison；(Neutral) 均保留 → 转用数据无关差异化（见下）；(Bad) 均丢失 → negative-as-contribution, scope SFT。**数据无关差异化（任何场景均可用）**：(i) ℓz* 有参数化 null (≈N(0,1), bootstrap 已验证) → 可直接假设检验, HT 无此性质；(ii) Snijders 校正补偿 θ 估计误差 (Var*=Var_l - C²/I(θ)), HT 无此校正；(iii) ℓz* 用 a/b/c/d 四参数加权 item 贡献, HT 仅用 b → MMLU 跨 57 科目 item 异质性大时 ℓz* 理论更精确。这些点不依赖 post-RL 结果，论文中应明确讨论。 | exp-baseline-comparison, exp-post-rl |\n| R13 | \"Minimal-information overstates\" | **[Dream D2 三档一致]** \"Minimal-information operating point\" obscures PSN-IRT 4PL parameter dependency. Reframe to \"minimal information **from the target model**\" or \"minimal runtime information\" — explicitly acknowledge PSN-IRT calibration as an external input requirement. | — |\n| R10 | \"Leaderboard audit baseline unreliable\" | Leaderboard audit abandoned (D011). ctrl-contam is the validated detection. 12-model case study uses PSN-IRT validated parameters directly (no baseline estimation needed). v1 data availability noted as future work. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R11 | \"Power function is upper bound\" | Report both theoretical upper bound AND adjusted power (memorization fraction from ctrl-contam seen/unseen split). Gap = SFT generalization effect quantification. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-power-theory |\n\n## Key Narrative Elements (from External Review + Distillation)\n\n1. **Detection frontier framing** — Systematically rank all methods by information access level (binary < rephrased retest < token probs < logits < weights). IRT-FIT defines the bottom of this frontier.\n2. **Definitional pivot (à la ConStat)** — \"All prior contamination detection methods require privileged access. We ask a more fundamental question: what can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" This reframes our work as problem reformulation, not just cross-domain transfer.\n3. **RL-robustness as structural advantage** — Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) proves all 10 log-prob methods ≈ random on RL-trained reasoning models. Person-fit operates on binary response patterns, not token distributions — structurally immune to RL-induced distributional shifts. This is our strongest motivation against log-prob baselines.\n4. **Scalability potential (deferred to future work)** — 13K+ v1 per-item data publicly available. IRT-FIT is uniquely suited for retrospective audit (only needs archival binary data). BUT: current paper does NOT include large-scale audit (D011: IRT refit failed). Mention data availability + roadmap in Discussion/Future Work. NEVER claim \"leaderboard audit\" or \"large-scale detection\" in current paper.\n5. **Inverted-U as empirical characterization** — Derive from: (a) contamination→0%: signal drowned in sampling noise; (b) contamination→100%: identifiability collapse. Simulation fit R²=0.957; real-data fit R²=0.65 (gap due to SFT generalization). Frame as \"empirical trend\" not \"theory/law.\"\n6. **Baseline comparison as evidence for model-level aggregation** — Item-level detection is near-random for ALL binary-only methods (including oracle RF). This is NOT a weakness — it reveals that contamination signal is diffuse (memorization fraction ~35%). Model-level lz* aggregates 14K weak signals into |d|>2.9. Frame item-level weakness as supporting evidence: \"any method that aggregates is better than any method that localizes.\" lz* vs Guttman/U3 8× gap proves IRT parameterization matters. acc z-score is sensitive but non-specific (sensitivity-specificity tradeoff).\n7. **Scope precision** — Target: \"intentional SFT contamination / leaderboard gaming\". Pretraining exposure → smooth distributional improvement, not in scope. Honest scoping > vague claims.\n8. **Terminology guard** — NEVER use \"binary information bottleneck\" or \"information-theoretic lower bound for all binary-only methods.\" We can only claim lz* (a specific statistic) has limitations under SFT generalization — NOT that all binary-only methods fail. Correct framing: \"IRT person-fit as a principled framework at the minimal-information operating point.\"\n9. **Memorization fraction cross-family consistency** — MF is 35–38% at 15% contamination across Qwen (0.38) and Llama (0.35), only 3pp difference. Consistency strengthens generalizability. MF may vary with contamination mechanism (full FT vs QLoRA), model capacity, and benchmark difficulty — acknowledge in Limitations as deployment bootstrapping problem.\n10. **Validation hierarchy** — ctrl-contam = primary validation (ground truth, same model clean vs contaminated); 12-model case study = empirical findings (no ground truth, but validated parameters); v1 data = future work roadmap. Paper structure should reflect this priority.\n9. **lz* measures memorization, not generalization** — lz* detects aberrant patterns (memorization signature), not smooth ability improvement (generalization). This is a feature: it distinguishes genuine learning from rote memorization. Power function gives upper bound; ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction.\n10. **Negative results as contributions** — D007 (universal misfit) and D008 (empirical null well-calibrated) are \"honest negative results that become positive contributions\": universal misfit is a novel finding about LLM response patterns; the simulation-reality gap motivates Δlz* and quantifies SFT generalization. D011 (MML-EM refit failure) is a methodological caveat (classical vs neural IRT sample requirements). D009 (item alignment) is a data engineering detail (1 sentence in Data section). Present negatives with the framing: \"the gap between where IRT works perfectly (simulation) and where it struggles (real LLM data) is itself informative.\"\n11. **ctrl-contam actual results (D015)** — contam_15 |d|=3.85 (strong), contam_50 non-monotonic under free-θ but **monotonic under θ-fixed** (ratio=2.93). θ-shift is the mechanism: contamination→higher θ_MLE→absorbs aberrance signal. Frame as \"principled detection with quantified operating characteristics + θ-shift boundary condition.\" Headline: \"We don't just detect — we characterize, including the conditions under which detection degrades.\" Do NOT claim \"state-of-the-art detection.\"\n12. **θ-shift as methodological contribution (D015)** — Person-fit sensitivity degrades when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data. This is a novel finding for contamination detection: (a) θ-fixed analysis recovers monotonic dose-response, (b) the θ-shift magnitude (0.47 at 50% contamination) quantifies the confound, (c) practical implication: use pre-contamination θ baseline or cross-validated θ. Present as a contribution, not a limitation.\n13. **Cross-family baseline lz* divergence (Reviewer WARNING)** — Clean lz* spans ~9σ: Qwen +8.68, Mistral +5.42, Llama -0.14. 固定阈值检测失效（Qwen contam_15 lz*=+3.85 仍为正值）。论文必须：(a) 明确 IRT-FIT 是相对检测（Δlz*/Cohen's d），非绝对阈值；(b) 展示 clean baseline lz* 跨家族差异表；(c) 预防性回答\"contam_15 lz*=+3.85 为正值为何算污染\"（因为 Δlz*=-4.83 是大效应）；(d) lz* baseline 作为\"模型内部一致性\"指标——Mistral acc 最低(0.514)但 lz* 第二高(+5.42)，说明 lz* 捕捉 difficulty-ordering 一致性而非准确率。\n14. **Inverted-U 是模型相关的** — Qwen 在 15%→50% 区间出现强 inversion（Δlz* 50%=-1.39 << 15%=-4.83），Llama 和 Mistral 在此区间 Δlz* 单调增大。Inverted-U 在 free-θ 下由 baseline misfit 调制——高 baseline lz* (Qwen +8.68) 的模型更容易出现 non-monotonicity。论文不能 claim inverted-U 为 universal phenomenon，需加 model-dependent caveat。θ-fixed 分析仍恢复所有家族的 monotonicity — 这是 θ-fixed 贡献的关键证据。\n15. **seen/unseen split as strongest signal** — contam_15 seen lz*≈0 (memorized items look \"normal\") vs unseen lz*=3.1. This is the clearest contamination fingerprint: items that should produce aberrant responses instead produce expected responses. More interpretable than aggregate Δlz*.\n\n## Writing Strategy (from Distillation)\n\n- **Story type**: \"跨界迁移型\" — unused in 0/8 peer papers. Our unique angle.\n- **Figure 1**: Problem illustration (dual-panel: contaminated vs clean response pattern). Use psychometric hook — impossible response pattern (hard items right, easy wrong).\n- **Contribution structure**: 3 contributions (method + characterization + empirical findings), escalating scope. Standard in 5/8 papers.\n- **Result tables**: Row=methods, col=datasets×metrics. Bold-best. Average column.\n- **Numbered findings**: Adopt PSN-IRT's \"Key Discoveries\" strategy for scannable presentation.\n- **CIs as differentiator**: 6/8 peer papers report no variance. Our bootstrap CIs are a competitive advantage.\n- **Baseline count**: Peer median ~5. Target ≥5 baselines.\n\n## Evidence Summary\n\n- **Phase A (simulation)**: Null check passed (4PL compatible with lz* theory). MMLU power@15%=97.9%. Power ∝ n_items confirmed. Simulation results stand — they establish theoretical detection capacity within the 4PL model.\n- **Phase B (real data)**: Gemini-1.5 MMLU acc=1.000, θ=0.78, lz*=+31.81. Cross-benchmark anomaly profiles identified.\n- **Empirical null analysis (exp-empirical-null)**: Bootstrap null calibration is benchmark-size dependent — large benchmarks well-calibrated (MMLU: mean bias 0.041, std 1.003, KS reject 8.3%; HellaSwag: 8.3%), small benchmarks poorly calibrated (HumanEval: 75%, ARC-C: 58.3%; overall KS reject 40%, 24/60). The statistical framework is sound for large benchmarks (n>10K). 57/60 real-data cells flagged because LLM lz* values are genuinely extreme (|lz*| >> 5) — this reflects **universal 4PL model misfit** (LLM response patterns violate IRT assumptions), not contamination-specific detection. **Important**: 57/60 vs accuracy z-score 4/60 demonstrates lz* captures response-pattern information beyond aggregate accuracy (evidence for Claim 3a universal misfit), NOT contamination detection superiority. Contamination detection evidence comes from simulation (lz* AUROC 0.675 vs ML 0.575 at 5%) and ctrl-contam (d=3.42, n=3, ddof=1, ℓz*-corrected).\n- **Calibration gap reframed (D007→D008)**: The gap is not \"null is biased\" but \"real LLM data genuinely deviates from 4PL\". This strengthens Δlz* approach: well-calibrated null means within-model shifts are statistically meaningful.\n- **Controlled contamination (exp-ctrl-contam-pilot, D015, ℓz*-corrected)**: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct × MMLU, 4 conditions (0%×3 seeds, 15%, 50%). **n=3 clean seeds (ℓz*-corrected)**: s1=9.47, s2=7.05, s3=9.53 (s2 outlier; mean=8.68, std=1.41). Key results: (a) contam_15 |Cohen's d|=3.42 (n=3, ddof=1, strong effect); (b) contam_50 |d|=0.99 (n=3, ddof=1, borderline large); (c) free-θ dose-response non-monotonic and more extreme after correction (contam_50 Δlz*=1.40 < contam_15 Δlz*=4.84, ratio=3.46) due to θ-shift confound; (d) **θ-fixed analysis (ℓz*-corrected)**: θ_fixed=-0.0965 (n=3 clean θ_MLE mean, unchanged by ℓz* correction); lz*_fixed: contam_15=11.852, contam_50=18.576; Δlz*_fixed: contam_15=+3.17, contam_50=+9.89; ratio=3.12 (virtually unchanged from uncorrected 3.12 — Snijders correction scales proportionally); (e) seen/unseen memorization fingerprint; (f) memorization_fraction=0.38 (15%) and 0.29 (50%). θ-shift mechanism: contamination raises θ_MLE, absorbing aberrance signal — this is a methodological contribution. **Note**: all values ℓz*-corrected (Snijders 2001); prior uncorrected ℓz values archived as *_lz_uncorrected.json.\n- **Cross-family validation (exp-ctrl-contam-llama, ℓz*-corrected)**: Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct × MMLU, 3+2 conditions. **n=3 clean seeds (ℓz*-corrected)**: s1=0.845, s2=-0.182, s3=-1.084 (mean=-0.14, std=0.97). contam_15 lz*=-2.992 (θ=-0.276), contam_50 lz*=-3.331 (θ=-0.149). Δlz*: contam_15=-3.84, contam_50=-4.18, both significant. **Cohen's d (n=3, ddof=1)**: contam_15 d=-2.95 (large), contam_50 d=-3.31 (large), monotonic (|d_50|>|d_15|) — contrasting Qwen's non-monotonicity. **Free-θ**: slight monotonicity (ratio=1.09), contrasting Qwen's strong non-monotonicity (ratio=3.46). **θ_fixed (θ=-0.666)**: lz*_fixed contam_15=0.959, contam_50=1.172; Δlz*_fixed=+0.114/+0.327; ratio=2.87 (enhances monotonicity). θ-shift mechanism universal: Δθ Llama 0.39/0.52, Qwen 0.29/0.47. Memorization fraction ~0.33-0.38. **Narrative**: Qwen story = \"θ_fixed repairs non-monotonicity\"; Llama story = \"θ_fixed enhances existing monotonicity\". Both confirm θ_fixed recovers/strengthens dose-response. Non-monotonicity is model-dependent (modulated by baseline misfit magnitude). Qwen clean lz*=8.68 vs Llama -0.14 — discuss in §6. **Cross-family Cohen's d summary**: Qwen d_15=-3.42/d_50=-0.99; Llama d_15=-2.95/d_50=-3.31. Both families |d|>2.9 at 15%, confirming detection generalizes.\n- **4PL real-data degradation**: 3PL(d=1) vs 4PL lz* correlation r=0.225, RMSE=68.41. d parameter essential for high-ability models (DeepSeek-V3 Δ=357). Complements simulation ablation (+14-27pp power gain).\n","numLines":92,"startLine":1,"totalLines":92}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014tr4W5MAEMP3NSckvug9vJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Controlled Contamination Pilot (Qwen)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B × 4 conditions (0%-seed1/0%-seed2/15%/50%) × MMLU only. Go/no-go 信号实验。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"clean_seed1_lz_star\": 8.5,\n7\t      \"clean_seed2_lz_star\": 7.9,\n8\t      \"clean_mean\": 8.2,\n9\t      \"clean_std\": 0.42,\n10\t      \"contam_15_lz_star\": 4.1,\n11\t      \"contam_50_lz_star\": 7.0,\n12\t      \"delta_lz_star_15\": -4.1,\n13\t      \"delta_lz_star_50\": -1.2,\n14\t      \"cohens_d_contam15\": -3.2,\n15\t      \"cohens_d_contam50\": -1.1,\n16\t      \"contam_15_acc\": 0.72,\n17\t      \"contam_50_acc\": 0.76,\n18\t      \"memorization_fraction_15\": 0.36,\n19\t      \"memorization_fraction_50\": 0.28,\n20\t      \"seen_lz_star_15\": 0.3,\n21\t      \"unseen_lz_star_15\": 3.2,\n22\t      \"theta_shift_15\": 0.25,\n23\t      \"theta_shift_50\": 0.45,\n24\t      \"theta_fixed_contam15_lz\": 11.5,\n25\t      \"theta_fixed_contam50_lz\": 17.8,\n26\t      \"theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.9\n27\t    },\n28\t    \"tables\": [\n29\t      {\n30\t        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen Pilot Controlled Contamination Results\",\n31\t        \"columns\": [\n32\t          \"condition\",\n33\t          \"lz_star\",\n34\t          \"delta_lz_star\",\n35\t          \"cohens_d\",\n36\t          \"acc\",\n37\t          \"theta_mle\",\n38\t          \"lz_star_fixed\",\n39\t          \"memo_frac\"\n40\t        ],\n41\t        \"rows\": [\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"clean_s1\",\n44\t            8.5,\n45\t            0,\n46\t            \"-\",\n47\t            0.678,\n48\t            -0.1,\n49\t            \"-\",\n50\t            \"-\"\n51\t          ],\n52\t          [\n53\t            \"clean_s2\",\n54\t            7.9,\n55\t            0,\n56\t            \"-\",\n57\t            0.676,\n58\t            -0.11,\n59\t            \"-\",\n60\t            \"-\"\n61\t          ],\n62\t          [\n63\t            \"contam_15\",\n64\t            4.1,\n65\t            -4.1,\n66\t            -3.2,\n67\t            0.72,\n68\t            0.15,\n69\t            11.5,\n70\t            0.36\n71\t          ],\n72\t          [\n73\t            \"contam_50\",\n74\t            7.0,\n75\t            -1.2,\n76\t            -1.1,\n77\t            0.76,\n78\t            0.35,\n79\t            17.8,\n80\t            0.28\n81\t          ]\n82\t        ]\n83\t      }\n84\t    ],\n85\t    \"figures\": [],\n86\t    \"analysis\": \"Go 信号确认。|d|>2 at 15% 足以支撑 Claim 1。Non-monotonicity 在 free-θ 下出现 是预期的，θ-fixed 恢复单调性是方法论贡献。Memorization fraction ~36% 与 SFT generalization 一致——QLoRA 仅记忆约 1/3 注入 items，其余通过泛化提升。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 Qwen 控制实验预期产生强效应但 free-θ 下 50% contamination 出现 non-monotonicity。Qwen baseline lz* 高 (~8-9) 因其 response pattern 与 4PL 预测高度一致但非完美匹配；15% 污染产生明显 aberrance（memorization fraction ~36% 意味着约 1/3 seen items 被记忆，产生 difficulty-inconsistent correct responses）。 50% 条件下 θ-shift 吸收大量 aberrance 信号导致 free-θ d 值下降至 ~1.1，但 θ-fixed 恢复单调性（ratio ~2.9）。这与 Qwen 高 baseline misfit (lz*~8.5) 交互——高 baseline 模型更容易出现 non-monotonicity 因为 θ 估计对 response pattern 变化更敏感。\\n\"\n87\t  },\n88\t  {\n89\t    \"name\": \"Full Controlled Contamination (4 Families)\",\n90\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B + Gemma-4-31B + Llama-3.1-8B + Mistral-7B-v0.3 × 6 levels (0/5/10/15/25/50%) × MMLU + GSM8K + HellaSwag。\\n\",\n91\t    \"results\": {\n92\t      \"n_families_validated\": 3,\n93\t      \"qwen_mmlu_d15\": -3.4,\n94\t      \"qwen_mmlu_d50\": -1.0,\n95\t      \"llama_mmlu_d15\": -2.9,\n96\t      \"llama_mmlu_d50\": -3.3,\n97\t      \"mistral_mmlu_d15\": -2.5,\n98\t      \"mistral_mmlu_d50\": -3.0,\n99\t      \"gemma_mmlu_d15\": -2.2,\n100\t      \"gemma_mmlu_d50\": -2.8,\n101\t      \"gemma_note\": \"Gemma 31B 参数量大，QLoRA 效率不同，可能需调参或 drop\",\n102\t      \"gsm8k_avg_d15\": -1.5,\n103\t      \"gsm8k_avg_d50\": -2.0,\n104\t      \"hellaswag_avg_d15\": -1.8,\n105\t      \"hellaswag_avg_d50\": -2.5,\n106\t      \"cross_family_memo_frac_range\": [\n107\t        0.3,\n108\t        0.4\n109\t      ],\n110\t      \"cross_family_memo_frac_mean\": 0.35,\n111\t      \"dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed\": true,\n112\t      \"dose_response_monotonic_free\": \"model-dependent\",\n113\t      \"n_conditions_total\": 72,\n114\t      \"n_conditions_significant\": 55,\n115\t      \"small_benchmark_weakness\": \"GSM8K (1319 items) d ~1.5 at 15%, below MMLU\"\n116\t    },\n117\t    \"tables\": [\n118\t      {\n119\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Family Detection Summary (MMLU, θ-free)\",\n120\t        \"columns\": [\n121\t          \"family\",\n122\t          \"clean_lz\",\n123\t          \"d_5pct\",\n124\t          \"d_10pct\",\n125\t          \"d_15pct\",\n126\t          \"d_25pct\",\n127\t          \"d_50pct\",\n128\t          \"memo_frac_15\"\n129\t        ],\n130\t        \"rows\": [\n131\t          [\n132\t            \"Qwen-7B\",\n133\t            8.7,\n134\t            -0.8,\n135\t            -1.8,\n136\t            -3.4,\n137\t            -2.8,\n138\t            -1.0,\n139\t            0.38\n140\t          ],\n141\t          [\n142\t            \"Llama-8B\",\n143\t            -0.1,\n144\t            -0.5,\n145\t            -1.5,\n146\t            -2.9,\n147\t            -3.1,\n148\t            -3.3,\n149\t            0.35\n150\t          ],\n151\t          [\n152\t            \"Mistral-7B\",\n153\t            5.4,\n154\t            -0.7,\n155\t            -1.6,\n156\t            -2.5,\n157\t            -2.8,\n158\t            -3.0,\n159\t            0.34\n160\t          ],\n161\t          [\n162\t            \"Gemma-31B\",\n163\t            3.2,\n164\t            -0.4,\n165\t            -1.0,\n166\t            -2.2,\n167\t            -2.5,\n168\t            -2.8,\n169\t            0.32\n170\t          ]\n171\t        ]\n172\t      },\n173\t      {\n174\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Benchmark Detection (15% contamination, all families avg)\",\n175\t        \"columns\": [\n176\t          \"benchmark\",\n177\t          \"n_items\",\n178\t          \"avg_d\",\n179\t          \"power_theory\",\n180\t          \"memo_frac\"\n181\t        ],\n182\t        \"rows\": [\n183\t          [\n184\t            \"MMLU\",\n185\t            14042,\n186\t            -2.8,\n187\t            0.979,\n188\t            0.35\n189\t          ],\n190\t          [\n191\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n192\t            10042,\n193\t            -1.8,\n194\t            0.753,\n195\t            0.33\n196\t          ],\n197\t          [\n198\t            \"GSM8K\",\n199\t            1319,\n200\t            -1.5,\n201\t            0.591,\n202\t            0.3\n203\t          ]\n204\t        ]\n205\t      }\n206\t    ],\n207\t    \"figures\": [],\n208\t    \"analysis\": \"3 families 足以支撑跨家族泛化 claim。Gemma 若部分失败，以 footnote 说明参数量/ QLoRA 差异。n_items 效应与 power theory 一致——这本身强化 Claim 2。Memorization fraction 跨家族一致性 (3pp 差异) 是关键发现，支撑 SFT 泛化机制的普适性。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 3/4 families 成功验证（n_families_validated=3）。Gemma-4-31B 因 参数量大且 QLoRA rank 可能不足，存在训练不稳定或效果弱化风险——median 档下 Gemma 可能仅提供 partial 结果或需 downgrade 为 supporting evidence。跨 benchmark 差异反映 n_items 效应（MMLU 14042 >> GSM8K 1319）——power theory 预测 GSM8K 在 15% 仅有 ~59% power，对应 d ~1.5。HellaSwag (10042 items) 介于两者 之间。Memorization fraction 跨家族一致 (~35%) 是 SFT 机制的稳定性质， 不依赖模型架构——QLoRA 的泛化模式相似因为都是 low-rank adaptation。Free-θ non-monotonicity 仅出现在高 baseline lz* 模型（Qwen, Mistral），Llama (baseline ~0) 保持单调。\\n\"\n209\t  },\n210\t  {\n211\t    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Audit (ABANDONED)\",\n212\t    \"description\": \"Open LLM Leaderboard v1 大规模扫描。已因 MML-EM refit 失败 (a_r=0.111) 而放弃。\\n\",\n213\t    \"results\": {\n214\t      \"status\": \"ABANDONED\",\n215\t      \"reason\": \"a_r=0.111 discrimination failure makes v1-refit IRT parameters unreliable\",\n216\t      \"data_availability_noted\": true,\n217\t      \"n_models_available\": \"13000+\",\n218\t      \"future_work_mention\": true\n219\t    },\n220\t    \"tables\": [],\n221\t    \"figures\": [],\n222\t    \"analysis\": \"放弃是正确决定。论文中将 refit 失败作为 methodological caveat (Claim 3c) 展示——量化经典 IRT 与 neural IRT 估计的 sample size gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下此实验不执行。MML-EM 从 N=63→178 模型重拟合 IRT 参数，discrimination 参数 a_r=0.111 远低于 0.2 阈值——经典 IRT 拟合方法在 LLM 数据上失效因为： (1) 样本量仍不足（经典 IRT 需 N>500），(2) LLM response pattern 违反 local independence（同 domain items 相关），(3) 模型能力分布与 IRT 假设不匹配。 13K+ 数据可用性写入 Discussion/Future Work 作为 scaling roadmap。\\n\"\n223\t  },\n224\t  {\n225\t    \"name\": \"Natural Experiment (v1 base→chat pairs)\",\n226\t    \"description\": \"v1 leaderboard base→chat model pairs 的 Δlz* 作为 SFT 效应代理。P2-optional。\\n\",\n227\t    \"results\": {\n228\t      \"n_pairs\": 21,\n229\t      \"n_complete_pairs\": 9,\n230\t      \"significant_benchmarks\": 2,\n231\t      \"hellaswag_mean_deviation\": -3.4,\n232\t      \"hellaswag_p\": 0.001,\n233\t      \"gsm8k_mean_deviation\": 3.9,\n234\t      \"gsm8k_p\": 0.009,\n235\t      \"mmlu_p\": 0.15,\n236\t      \"arcc_p\": 0.38,\n237\t      \"individual_outliers\": 0,\n238\t      \"interpretation\": \"systematic SFT effects, not contamination-specific\"\n239\t    },\n240\t    \"tables\": [\n241\t      {\n242\t        \"name\": \"Table: Natural Experiment SFT Effects\",\n243\t        \"columns\": [\n244\t          \"benchmark\",\n245\t          \"mean_delta_lz\",\n246\t          \"t_stat\",\n247\t          \"p_value\",\n248\t          \"interpretation\"\n249\t        ],\n250\t        \"rows\": [\n251\t          [\n252\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n253\t            -3.4,\n254\t            -3.97,\n255\t            0.001,\n256\t            \"SFT decreases person-fit\"\n257\t          ],\n258\t          [\n259\t            \"GSM8K\",\n260\t            3.9,\n261\t            3.35,\n262\t            0.009,\n263\t            \"SFT increases person-fit\"\n264\t          ],\n265\t          [\n266\t            \"MMLU\",\n267\t            \"+1.2\",\n268\t            1.54,\n269\t            0.15,\n270\t            \"n.s.\"\n271\t          ],\n272\t          [\n273\t            \"ARC-C\",\n274\t            \"-0.8\",\n275\t            -0.91,\n276\t            0.38,\n277\t            \"n.s.\"\n278\t          ]\n279\t        ]\n280\t      }\n281\t    ],\n282\t    \"figures\": [],\n283\t    \"analysis\": \"Supplementary evidence only。系统性 SFT 方向差异 (HellaSwag↓, GSM8K↑) 有趣 但因 refit 参数质量问题不做强 claim。P2 降级合理。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 显示系统性 SFT 效应（方向一致的 Δlz* shift） 但无个体 pair 出现 benchmark-specific 异常。这是因为 chat 模型的 SFT 训练 普遍改变了 response pattern——HellaSwag (commonsense) 受 instruction tuning 负面影响（降低 person-fit），GSM8K (math) 受益（提高 person-fit）。但用 a_r=0.111 的 refit 参数计算的 lz* 本质上退化为 accuracy-like 指标，无法 区分 contamination 与 legitimate SFT improvement。仅 9 个 complete pairs 缺乏统计检验力做细粒度分析。作为 P2 supplementary evidence 足够。\\n\"\n284\t  },\n285\t  {\n286\t    \"name\": \"v1 IRT Refit Expanded (N≥500)\",\n287\t    \"description\": \"扩大 v1 IRT 重拟合样本量至 N≥500，最终关闭 Path D。\\n\",\n288\t    \"results\": {\n289\t      \"n_models_downloaded\": 178,\n290\t      \"a_pearson_r_3pl\": 0.127,\n291\t      \"a_pearson_r_2pl\": -0.029,\n292\t      \"b_pearson_r_3pl\": 0.663,\n293\t      \"conclusion\": \"Path D dead — discrimination failure persists at N=178\",\n294\t      \"threshold_met\": false\n295\t    },\n296\t    \"tables\": [\n297\t      {\n298\t        \"name\": \"Table: IRT Refit Parameter Recovery\",\n299\t        \"columns\": [\n300\t          \"method\",\n301\t          \"n_models\",\n302\t          \"a_r\",\n303\t          \"b_r\",\n304\t          \"conclusion\"\n305\t        ],\n306\t        \"rows\": [\n307\t          [\n308\t            \"3PL pilot\",\n309\t            63,\n310\t            0.111,\n311\t            0.626,\n312\t            \"dead\"\n313\t          ],\n314\t          [\n315\t            \"3PL expanded\",\n316\t            178,\n317\t            0.127,\n318\t            0.663,\n319\t            \"dead\"\n320\t          ],\n321\t          [\n322\t            \"2PL expanded\",\n323\t            178,\n324\t            -0.029,\n325\t            0.572,\n326\t            \"dead\"\n327\t          ]\n328\t        ]\n329\t      }\n330\t    ],\n331\t    \"figures\": [],\n332\t    \"analysis\": \"Path D 最终关闭。论文 Claim 3c 中作为 methodological caveat 展示。 关键贡献：量化经典 IRT 与 LLM context 的 sample size gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 N=178 仍无法恢复 discrimination 参数（a_r=0.127, 远低于 0.4 可行阈值）。根本原因不是样本量而是经典 MML-EM 拟合方法的结构性限制： (1) LLM response pattern 不满足 local independence——同 domain 1000+ items 高度相关，(2) 能力维度 θ 对 LLM 而言不是单一维度——不同 benchmark 需要不同 \\\"能力\\\"，(3) N=178 模型虽多于 pilot 的 63，但 item 数 14042 远超模型数， 导致 over-determined 系统。b_r=0.663 部分成功因为 difficulty 与 accuracy 线性相关——即使模型不多也能恢复。a (discrimination) 需要建模 item 间差异化 响应概率的曲率，这需要更多分布覆盖。Path D 确认关闭。\\n\"\n333\t  },\n334\t  {\n335\t    \"name\": \"4PL vs 3PL Ablation\",\n336\t    \"description\": \"4PL vs 3PL(d=1) ablation——量化 feasibility parameter d 对检测的影响。\\n\",\n337\t    \"results\": {\n338\t      \"far_4pl\": 0.05,\n339\t      \"far_3pl\": \"4.7-16.5%\",\n340\t      \"far_2pl\": \"50-100%\",\n341\t      \"mean_power_gain_mmlu\": \"+27pp\",\n342\t      \"mean_power_gain_hellaswag\": \"+26pp\",\n343\t      \"mean_power_gain_gsm8k\": \"+20pp\",\n344\t      \"items_with_d_lt_0.95_mmlu\": \"46%\",\n345\t      \"max_power_gain\": \"+59pp (HellaSwag)\",\n346\t      \"deepseek_v3_delta\": 357\n347\t    },\n348\t    \"tables\": [\n349\t      {\n350\t        \"name\": \"Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Power (25% contamination)\",\n351\t        \"columns\": [\n352\t          \"benchmark\",\n353\t          \"power_4pl\",\n354\t          \"power_3pl\",\n355\t          \"gain\",\n356\t          \"pct_items_d_lt_0.95\"\n357\t        ],\n358\t        \"rows\": [\n359\t          [\n360\t            \"MMLU\",\n361\t            0.776,\n362\t            0.329,\n363\t            \"+44.7pp\",\n364\t            \"46%\"\n365\t          ],\n366\t          [\n367\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n368\t            0.534,\n369\t            0.28,\n370\t            \"+25.4pp\",\n371\t            \"38%\"\n372\t          ],\n373\t          [\n374\t            \"GSM8K\",\n375\t            0.73,\n376\t            0.334,\n377\t            \"+39.6pp\",\n378\t            \"42%\"\n379\t          ],\n380\t          [\n381\t            \"ARC-C\",\n382\t            0.132,\n383\t            0.091,\n384\t            \"+4.1pp\",\n385\t            \"28%\"\n386\t          ],\n387\t          [\n388\t            \"HumanEval\",\n389\t            0.318,\n390\t            0.165,\n391\t            \"+15.3pp\",\n392\t            \"35%\"\n393\t          ]\n394\t        ]\n395\t      }\n396\t    ],\n397\t    \"figures\": [],\n398\t    \"analysis\": \"4PL 对 LLM 应用必要性的强证据。回应 R8 reviewer concern。结论：使用 3PL 会丢失约一半检测力。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 4PL d 参数对检测至关重要。46% MMLU items 有 d<0.95——这些 items 的 upper asymptote 低于 1.0，意味着即使能力极高的模型也无法以 100% 概率答对。 忽略 d (设 d=1) 使得 4PL 模型对高能力模型的预测概率系统性偏高，产生虚假 aberrance 信号——高能力模型答错一个 d=0.8 的 item 是正常的，但 3PL 认为是 异常。结果：(1) 3PL FAR 膨胀至 4.7-16.5%（benchmark 依赖），(2) detection power 平均下降 20-27pp 因为 noise floor 升高，(3) 2PL 更灾难性（FAR 50-100%） 因为同时忽略了 guessing parameter c。power gain 在 d<0.8 bucket 最大 (+6.8 to +61.2pp)，d≥0.95 时 gain 可忽略。这证明 PSN-IRT 的 4PL 参数化对 LLM contamination detection 而非 academic nicety 是必要的。\\n\"\n399\t  },\n400\t  {\n401\t    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison (≥5 baselines)\",\n402\t    \"description\": \"在控制实验 ground-truth contaminated models 上比较 IRT-FIT vs ≥5 baselines。 包括 ConStat (retest), Min-K%++ (token probs), acc z-score, HT, Guttman/U3。\\n\",\n403\t    \"results\": {\n404\t      \"model_level_lz_star_d_qwen15\": -3.42,\n405\t      \"model_level_ht_d_qwen15\": -3.21,\n406\t      \"model_level_guttman_d_qwen15\": -0.43,\n407\t      \"model_level_u3_d_qwen15\": -0.38,\n408\t      \"model_level_acc_zscore\": 160.6,\n409\t      \"ht_vs_lz_star_ratio\": 0.94,\n410\t      \"lz_star_vs_guttman_ratio\": 8.0,\n411\t      \"constat_retest_auroc\": 0.78,\n412\t      \"mink_sft_auroc\": 0.6,\n413\t      \"item_level_max_auroc\": 0.63,\n414\t      \"item_level_lz_itemwise_auroc\": 0.536,\n415\t      \"item_level_irt_residual_auroc\": 0.582,\n416\t      \"item_level_lr_cross_auroc\": 0.592,\n417\t      \"item_level_rf_oracle_auroc\": 0.63,\n418\t      \"n_baselines_beaten\": 4,\n419\t      \"n_baselines_total\": 6\n420\t    },\n421\t    \"tables\": [\n422\t      {\n423\t        \"name\": \"Table: Model-Level Baseline Comparison (Qwen 15% contamination)\",\n424\t        \"columns\": [\n425\t          \"method\",\n426\t          \"info_required\",\n427\t          \"cohens_d\",\n428\t          \"requires_retest\",\n429\t          \"interpretable\"\n430\t        ],\n431\t        \"rows\": [\n432\t          [\n433\t            \"lz* (ours)\",\n434\t            \"binary + 4PL params\",\n435\t            -3.42,\n436\t            \"No\",\n437\t            \"Yes (θ-shift, memo frac)\"\n438\t          ],\n439\t          [\n440\t            \"HT\",\n441\t            \"binary + item difficulty\",\n442\t            -3.21,\n443\t            \"No\",\n444\t            \"Limited\"\n445\t          ],\n446\t          [\n447\t            \"Guttman\",\n448\t            \"binary only\",\n449\t            -0.43,\n450\t            \"No\",\n451\t            \"No\"\n452\t          ],\n453\t          [\n454\t            \"U3\",\n455\t            \"binary only\",\n456\t            -0.38,\n457\t            \"No\",\n458\t            \"No\"\n459\t          ],\n460\t          [\n461\t            \"acc z-score\",\n462\t            \"binary + population stats\",\n463\t            -160.6,\n464\t            \"No\",\n465\t            \"No (specificity issue)\"\n466\t          ],\n467\t          [\n468\t            \"ConStat\",\n469\t            \"binary + retest\",\n470\t            \"AUROC=0.78\",\n471\t            \"Yes\",\n472\t            \"Partial\"\n473\t          ],\n474\t          [\n475\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n476\t            \"token probabilities\",\n477\t            \"AUROC=0.60\",\n478\t            \"No\",\n479\t            \"No\"\n480\t          ]\n481\t        ]\n482\t      },\n483\t      {\n484\t        \"name\": \"Table: Item-Level Detection (all methods near-random)\",\n485\t        \"columns\": [\n486\t          \"method\",\n487\t          \"auroc_qwen15\",\n488\t          \"auroc_qwen50\",\n489\t          \"auroc_llama15\",\n490\t          \"auroc_llama50\"\n491\t        ],\n492\t        \"rows\": [\n493\t          [\n494\t            \"lz_itemwise\",\n495\t            0.536,\n496\t            0.535,\n497\t            0.528,\n498\t            0.536\n499\t          ],\n500\t          [\n501\t            \"irt_residual\",\n502\t            0.578,\n503\t            0.563,\n504\t            0.582,\n505\t            0.581\n506\t          ],\n507\t          [\n508\t            \"lr_cross_model\",\n509\t            0.586,\n510\t            0.567,\n511\t            0.592,\n512\t            0.585\n513\t          ],\n514\t          [\n515\t            \"rf_oracle\",\n516\t            0.61,\n517\t            0.63,\n518\t            0.615,\n519\t            0.629\n520\t          ],\n521\t          [\n522\t            \"random\",\n523\t            0.5,\n524\t            0.5,\n525\t            0.5,\n526\t            0.5\n527\t          ]\n528\t        ]\n529\t      }\n530\t    ],\n531\t    \"figures\": [],\n532\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档叙事转向：lz* 的优势不在 raw detection power（HT comparable）而在 interpretability 和 framework contribution。n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT comparable 但缺乏 parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting——这些在 MMLU 57 subjects 异质性大时理论上更精确。 ConStat 有效但需 retest (更多信息)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心发现：HT 与 lz* 在 model-level detection 上差距很小 (d ratio ~0.94)——HT 仅需 item difficulty，无需完整 4PL 参数化，却达到 comparable 效果。这是因为 model-level aggregation 对 14K items 的 central limit theorem 效应使得 item-level 参数权重差异被平均掉——HT 的 uniform weighting 与 lz* 的 a-weighted 方案在大 n 下收敛。lz* vs Guttman/U3 的 8× 差距证明 IRT 框架（含 difficulty ordering）优于纯 response pattern 统计。 ConStat retest AUROC=0.78 有效但需额外推理轮次（更多信息），符合 detection frontier 叙事。Min-K%++ 在 SFT 上 AUROC=0.60（弱），因为 SFT 改变了 token 分布但未产生 memorization-specific 的 perplexity 异常——SFT 后模型对 contaminated items 的 logprob 分布与 generalization 难以区分。Item-level 所有方法 near-random (max 0.63 with oracle) 因为 memorization fraction ~35% 意味着仅 1/3 items 产生可检测信号——这种 diffuse signature 只能通过 model-level aggregation 检测。acc z-score 的 z=160 说明它在 controlled setting 下 trivially 有效但无法在 real-world 中区分 contamination 与 legitimate high ability。\\n\"\n533\t  },\n534\t  {\n535\t    \"name\": \"Multiscale lzm Aggregation\",\n536\t    \"description\": \"实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合的 标准化 lz* 总分。\\n\",\n537\t    \"results\": {\n538\t      \"lzm_gemini15\": 45.2,\n539\t      \"lzm_deepseek_v3\": 38.7,\n540\t      \"lzm_qwen_plus\": 35.1,\n541\t      \"lzm_doubao\": -18.3,\n542\t      \"lzm_mistral\": 12.4,\n543\t      \"lzm_correlation_with_max_lz\": 0.92,\n544\t      \"lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_clean\": 12.8,\n545\t      \"lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_15\": 6.5,\n546\t      \"lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_50\": 9.2,\n547\t      \"added_value_over_per_benchmark\": \"marginal\"\n548\t    },\n549\t    \"tables\": [\n550\t      {\n551\t        \"name\": \"Table: lzm vs max-benchmark lz* (PSN-IRT 12 models)\",\n552\t        \"columns\": [\n553\t          \"model\",\n554\t          \"lzm\",\n555\t          \"max_lz_star\",\n556\t          \"dominant_benchmark\"\n557\t        ],\n558\t        \"rows\": [\n559\t          [\n560\t            \"Gemini-1.5\",\n561\t            45.2,\n562\t            31.8,\n563\t            \"MMLU\"\n564\t          ],\n565\t          [\n566\t            \"DeepSeek-V3\",\n567\t            38.7,\n568\t            25.3,\n569\t            \"MMLU\"\n570\t          ],\n571\t          [\n572\t            \"Qwen-Plus\",\n573\t            35.1,\n574\t            24.5,\n575\t            \"MMLU\"\n576\t          ],\n577\t          [\n578\t            \"Doubao-Pro\",\n579\t            -18.3,\n580\t            -15.2,\n581\t            \"HellaSwag\"\n582\t          ]\n583\t        ]\n584\t      }\n585\t    ],\n586\t    \"figures\": [],\n587\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix material。lzm 在当前数据条件下不改变结论。未来若覆盖更多 benchmarks 且有 cross-benchmark differential contamination，lzm 可显示独立价值。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 lzm 提供 per-model 的单一污染严重度指标，但 added value 有限。 lzm 本质是各 benchmark lz* 的 variance-weighted sum——由于 MMLU lz* 已经 dominate (n=14042 产生最极端值)，lzm 高度相关于 max per-benchmark lz* (r=0.92)。在 PSN-IRT 12-model data 上，lzm 重现已知排序（Gemini-1.5 最高）。 在 ctrl-contam 上，因为只有 MMLU 数据，lzm 退化为 lz* itself。理论贡献： 展示 Hong et al. 公式对 LLM multi-benchmark 评估的适用性。但 median 档下 不产生 new insight——P2 优先级合理。若 full ctrl-contam 覆盖 3 benchmarks， lzm 可显示跨 benchmark aggregation 的 marginal gain。\\n\"\n588\t  },\n589\t  {\n590\t    \"name\": \"Post-RL Hypothesis Test\",\n591\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B 先 SFT 污染再 GRPO 训练，测试 person-fit 是否在 RL 后保持检测力。\\n\",\n592\t    \"results\": {\n593\t      \"post_rl_lz_star_cohens_d\": 1.5,\n594\t      \"post_rl_ht_cohens_d\": 1.3,\n595\t      \"post_rl_mia_auroc\": 0.52,\n596\t      \"post_rl_mink_auroc\": 0.51,\n597\t      \"pre_rl_lz_star_d\": -3.42,\n598\t      \"signal_retention_lz\": 0.44,\n599\t      \"signal_retention_ht\": 0.4,\n600\t      \"rl_steps\": 2000,\n601\t      \"reward_type\": \"rule-based (accuracy on held-out)\",\n602\t      \"delta_lz_pre_rl\": -4.84,\n603\t      \"delta_lz_post_rl\": -2.1,\n604\t      \"delta_ht_post_rl\": -1.8,\n605\t      \"theta_shift_post_rl\": 0.35,\n606\t      \"acc_post_rl\": 0.74,\n607\t      \"acc_seen_post_rl\": 0.7,\n608\t      \"acc_unseen_post_rl\": 0.68,\n609\t      \"memo_frac_post_rl\": 0.12\n610\t    },\n611\t    \"tables\": [\n612\t      {\n613\t        \"name\": \"Table: Post-RL Detection Power Comparison\",\n614\t        \"columns\": [\n615\t          \"method\",\n616\t          \"pre_rl_d\",\n617\t          \"post_rl_d\",\n618\t          \"retention\",\n619\t          \"info_level\"\n620\t        ],\n621\t        \"rows\": [\n622\t          [\n623\t            \"lz*\",\n624\t            -3.42,\n625\t            -1.5,\n626\t            \"44%\",\n627\t            \"binary + 4PL\"\n628\t          ],\n629\t          [\n630\t            \"HT\",\n631\t            -3.21,\n632\t            -1.3,\n633\t            \"40%\",\n634\t            \"binary + difficulty\"\n635\t          ],\n636\t          [\n637\t            \"Guttman\",\n638\t            -0.43,\n639\t            -0.2,\n640\t            \"47%\",\n641\t            \"binary only\"\n642\t          ],\n643\t          [\n644\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n645\t            \"AUROC=0.60\",\n646\t            \"AUROC=0.51\",\n647\t            \"~random\",\n648\t            \"token probs\"\n649\t          ],\n650\t          [\n651\t            \"MIA-loss\",\n652\t            \"AUROC=0.59\",\n653\t            \"AUROC=0.52\",\n654\t            \"~random\",\n655\t            \"token probs\"\n656\t          ]\n657\t        ]\n658\t      },\n659\t      {\n660\t        \"name\": \"Table: Memorization Fraction Degradation\",\n661\t        \"columns\": [\n662\t          \"stage\",\n663\t          \"memo_frac\",\n664\t          \"lz_star\",\n665\t          \"delta_lz\",\n666\t          \"cohens_d\"\n667\t        ],\n668\t        \"rows\": [\n669\t          [\n670\t            \"clean\",\n671\t            \"-\",\n672\t            8.68,\n673\t            0,\n674\t            \"-\"\n675\t          ],\n676\t          [\n677\t            \"post-SFT (15%)\",\n678\t            0.38,\n679\t            3.85,\n680\t            -4.84,\n681\t            -3.42\n682\t          ],\n683\t          [\n684\t            \"post-RL\",\n685\t            0.12,\n686\t            6.58,\n687\t            -2.1,\n688\t            -1.5\n689\t          ]\n690\t        ]\n691\t      }\n692\t    ],\n693\t    \"figures\": [],\n694\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档叙事策略：(1) person-fit FAMILY 在 post-RL 保留 detectable signal (d>1.0)，log-prob 方法完全失效——class-level advantage 确认；(2) lz* 与 HT 退化幅度相似，无法 empirically differentiate——转用数据无关差异化论证 (parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting)；(3) memorization fraction 从 38%→12% 量化了 RL 的 \\\"washing\\\" 效应——这本身是对 RL alignment 文献的贡献（RL 部分消除 SFT contamination）；(4) 论文 claim 从 \\\"lz* uniquely robust\\\" 软化为 \\\"person-fit family robust; lz* uniquely interpretable\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：post-RL signal partially degrades for ALL person-fit methods。 GRPO 优化使模型学会\\\"推理\\\"而非\\\"记忆\\\"——RL 的 reward signal 鼓励 generalizable reasoning patterns，这部分平滑了 SFT 注入的 memorization fingerprint。 具体机制：(1) memorization fraction 从 ~38% 降至 ~12%——RL 使模型对 seen items 的回答方式从 rote recall 转向 reasoning-based，部分 items 不再产生 difficulty-inconsistent response；(2) θ 进一步上升（RL 提升整体能力），吸收 更多 aberrance；(3) 但 ~12% items 仍保留 memorization signature——这些是 factual knowledge items 无法通过推理路径解答，只能靠记忆。lz* d=1.5 和 HT d=1.3 均在 [1.0, 2.0] 范围内——detectable 但 effect size 明显弱于 pre-RL。 两者退化幅度相似（signal_retention ~40-44%），说明 RL-induced degradation 作用于 response pattern level（person-fit 家族共享），非统计量特异性。MIA/ Min-K++ AUROC ~0.51-0.52（near random）符合 Wang et al. 发现——log-prob 方法在 RL 后完全失效，而 person-fit 保留 partial signal。这是 person-fit 作为 family 的 structural advantage，但无法 differentiate lz* vs HT。\\n\"\n695\t  },\n696\t  {\n697\t    \"name\": \"Extra Benchmarks (BBH + MATH)\",\n698\t    \"description\": \"扩展 benchmark 覆盖：BBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 填充 1K-10K items 的 power gap。\\n\",\n699\t    \"results\": {\n700\t      \"bbh_4pl_available\": false,\n701\t      \"math_4pl_available\": false,\n702\t      \"bbh_2pl_refit_attempted\": true,\n703\t      \"bbh_a_r\": 0.15,\n704\t      \"math_a_r\": 0.12,\n705\t      \"bbh_power_15pct_sim\": 0.68,\n706\t      \"math_power_15pct_sim\": 0.62,\n707\t      \"bbh_ctrl_contam_d15\": -1.8,\n708\t      \"math_ctrl_contam_d15\": -1.2,\n709\t      \"power_gap_filled\": \"partial\",\n710\t      \"n_items_range_covered\": \"1319 (GSM8K) → 6511 (BBH) → 10042 (HellaSwag) → 14042 (MMLU)\"\n711\t    },\n712\t    \"tables\": [\n713\t      {\n714\t        \"name\": \"Table: Power Function Validation Across Benchmark Sizes\",\n715\t        \"columns\": [\n716\t          \"benchmark\",\n717\t          \"n_items\",\n718\t          \"power_theory_15pct\",\n719\t          \"power_sim_15pct\",\n720\t          \"power_ctrl_d15\"\n721\t        ],\n722\t        \"rows\": [\n723\t          [\n724\t            \"ARC-C\",\n725\t            295,\n726\t            0.129,\n727\t            0.129,\n728\t            \"0.5-1.5 (θ-fixed)\"\n729\t          ],\n730\t          [\n731\t            \"GSM8K\",\n732\t            1319,\n733\t            0.591,\n734\t            0.591,\n735\t            \"-1.5\"\n736\t          ],\n737\t          [\n738\t            \"MATH\",\n739\t            5000,\n740\t            0.62,\n741\t            \"~0.62 (sim)\",\n742\t            \"-1.2\"\n743\t          ],\n744\t          [\n745\t            \"BBH\",\n746\t            6511,\n747\t            0.68,\n748\t            \"~0.68 (sim)\",\n749\t            \"-1.8\"\n750\t          ],\n751\t          [\n752\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n753\t            10042,\n754\t            0.753,\n755\t            0.753,\n756\t            \"-1.8\"\n757\t          ],\n758\t          [\n759\t            \"MMLU\",\n760\t            14042,\n761\t            0.979,\n762\t            0.979,\n763\t            \"-3.4\"\n764\t          ]\n765\t        ]\n766\t      }\n767\t    ],\n768\t    \"figures\": [],\n769\t    \"analysis\": \"Partial contribution。Power theory 插值验证有效但缺乏 PSN-IRT 级别的 4PL ground truth。若 PSN-IRT authors 有 BBH/MATH 参数可协作获取——否则仅报告 simulation-based 预测。P2 优先级合理——非论文核心但强化 Claim 2。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 PSN-IRT 不包含 BBH/MATH 的 4PL 参数——需自行拟合。但自行 拟合面临与 v1-refit 相同的问题：discrimination recovery 弱 (a_r ~0.12-0.15)。 Workaround：(1) 仅用 simulation（假设合理 4PL 参数分布）预测 power—— BBH 6511 items 在 15% 时 power ~68%（power theory R²=0.957 插值）， MATH 5000 items ~62%；(2) 如果有 ctrl-contam 数据，用 PSN-IRT MMLU 参数 的 distributional statistics 生成 synthetic 4PL 参数估计。Ctrl-contam 实际 d 值偏低 (BBH d ~1.8, MATH d ~1.2) 因为拟合参数质量不如 PSN-IRT——但仍 在 detectable 范围。填充 power gap 是 partial 的：power theory 插值有效， 但缺乏 ground-truth 4PL 参数的直接验证。\\n\"\n770\t  },\n771\t  {\n772\t    \"name\": \"Domain-Level Analysis (MMLU subjects)\",\n773\t    \"description\": \"按 MMLU subject category 分别计算 person-fit，识别污染的 domain 分布模式。\\n\",\n774\t    \"results\": {\n775\t      \"gemini_accuracy\": 1.0,\n776\t      \"gemini_subjects_flagged\": \"50/57\",\n777\t      \"gemini_domain_concentrated\": false,\n778\t      \"gemini_stem_lz\": 21.2,\n779\t      \"gemini_humanities_lz\": 17.9,\n780\t      \"gemini_social_sciences_lz\": 15.9,\n781\t      \"gemini_other_lz\": 15.3,\n782\t      \"doubao_negative_lz\": true,\n783\t      \"doubao_stem_lz\": -2.0,\n784\t      \"doubao_humanities_lz\": -13.0,\n785\t      \"doubao_social_sciences_lz\": -14.8,\n786\t      \"ctrl_contam_domain_uniform\": true,\n787\t      \"ctrl_contam_seen_unseen_per_domain\": \"consistent across domains\"\n788\t    },\n789\t    \"tables\": [\n790\t      {\n791\t        \"name\": \"Table: Domain-Level lz* Profile (Selected Models)\",\n792\t        \"columns\": [\n793\t          \"model\",\n794\t          \"STEM\",\n795\t          \"Humanities\",\n796\t          \"Social_Sci\",\n797\t          \"Other\",\n798\t          \"pattern\"\n799\t        ],\n800\t        \"rows\": [\n801\t          [\n802\t            \"Gemini-1.5\",\n803\t            21.2,\n804\t            17.9,\n805\t            15.9,\n806\t            15.3,\n807\t            \"uniform high\"\n808\t          ],\n809\t          [\n810\t            \"Doubao-Pro\",\n811\t            -2.0,\n812\t            -13.0,\n813\t            -14.8,\n814\t            4.4,\n815\t            \"selective negative\"\n816\t          ],\n817\t          [\n818\t            \"Hunyuan-Large\",\n819\t            1.8,\n820\t            8.5,\n821\t            13.9,\n822\t            6.2,\n823\t            \"social science high\"\n824\t          ],\n825\t          [\n826\t            \"Yi-Lightning\",\n827\t            48.2,\n828\t            35.1,\n829\t            42.5,\n830\t            38.9,\n831\t            \"uniform extreme\"\n832\t          ]\n833\t        ]\n834\t      }\n835\t    ],\n836\t    \"figures\": [],\n837\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix or §5.3 subsection。Domain-level 分析支撑 Claim 3b (anomaly profiles)。Selective vs uniform 模式为 contamination typology 提供 mechanistic insight。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 domain analysis 确认两种 contamination 模式：(1) Gemini-1.5 的 uniform 高 lz* 横跨 50/57 subjects——全面 contamination 或极高能力 (acc=100%)，无法区分但 domain 均匀性本身是 pattern；(2) Doubao 的 selective negative lz*——Humanities/Social Sciences 显示强 negative aberrance (lz* -13 to -15)，暗示这些 domains 的 training data 与 MMLU item distribution 不匹配（答对 hard items 但答错 easy items）。STEM 相对正常 因为 STEM 训练数据覆盖更广。ctrl-contam (QLoRA) 注入的 items 按 random 15% 采样，因此 domain 分布预期 uniform——验证实验设计的内部一致性。 Domain-level 分析的附加价值：为 future auditors 提供 \\\"contamination fingerprinting\\\" 工具——selective domain contamination 暗示 targeted training。\\n\"\n838\t  },\n839\t  {\n840\t    \"name\": \"ConStat Comparison (Retest-Based)\",\n841\t    \"description\": \"ConStat (NeurIPS 2024) retest-based comparison on ctrl-contam models。 Part of baseline comparison but requiring additional inference runs。\\n\",\n842\t    \"results\": {\n843\t      \"constat_retest_auroc\": 0.78,\n844\t      \"constat_n_retests\": 3,\n845\t      \"constat_gpu_hours\": 8,\n846\t      \"constat_vs_lz_star_at_model_level\": \"comparable detection\",\n847\t      \"constat_information_cost\": \"3× inference budget\",\n848\t      \"constat_specificity\": \"higher than acc z-score\"\n849\t    },\n850\t    \"tables\": [],\n851\t    \"figures\": [],\n852\t    \"analysis\": \"Integrated into baseline comparison table。ConStat 结果强化 detection frontier 叙事——更多信息确实有帮助但 marginal gain 不大。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 ConStat 在 model-level 检测上 AUROC=0.78——有效但不如 lz* 的 d=3.4 直接。ConStat 的 retest 设计需要 rephrased items 和多次推理， 本质上是用\\\"更多信息\\\"换取\\\"更确定的判断\\\"。AUROC 0.78 而非更高是因为： (1) QLoRA SFT 的 memorization 是 partial (~35%)——rephrased items 的 response 变化不如 verbatim 记忆那么 dramatic；(2) SFT 泛化效应使得部分 seen items 即使 rephrased 也答对——这降低了 retest 的 sensitivity。 关键对比：lz* 用 zero 额外推理达到 comparable 检测力——这是 minimal-information operating point 的核心价值。ConStat 在 detection frontier 上位于 \\\"binary + retest\\\" 层级，高于 lz* 的 \\\"binary only\\\" 但低于 \\\"token probs\\\" 层级。\\n\"\n853\t  },\n854\t  {\n855\t    \"name\": \"MIA/Min-K++ on SFT Contamination\",\n856\t    \"description\": \"Min-K%++ 和 MIA-loss 在 SFT-contaminated 模型上的表现。\\n\",\n857\t    \"results\": {\n858\t      \"mink_sft_auroc\": 0.61,\n859\t      \"mia_loss_sft_auroc\": 0.59,\n860\t      \"mink_base_auroc\": 0.49,\n861\t      \"mia_loss_base_auroc\": 0.49,\n862\t      \"mink_post_rl_auroc\": 0.51,\n863\t      \"interpretation\": \"SFT produces weak token-level signal, RL washes it\"\n864\t    },\n865\t    \"tables\": [\n866\t      {\n867\t        \"name\": \"Table: Token-Level Methods Across Training Stages\",\n868\t        \"columns\": [\n869\t          \"method\",\n870\t          \"base_auroc\",\n871\t          \"sft_auroc\",\n872\t          \"post_rl_auroc\"\n873\t        ],\n874\t        \"rows\": [\n875\t          [\n876\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n877\t            0.49,\n878\t            0.61,\n879\t            0.51\n880\t          ],\n881\t          [\n882\t            \"MIA-loss\",\n883\t            0.49,\n884\t            0.59,\n885\t            0.52\n886\t          ],\n887\t          [\n888\t            \"PPL-based\",\n889\t            0.5,\n890\t            0.56,\n891\t            0.5\n892\t          ]\n893\t        ]\n894\t      }\n895\t    ],\n896\t    \"figures\": [],\n897\t    \"analysis\": \"Confirms binary-only person-fit is NOT inferior to token-prob methods for SFT contamination。Token methods' weakness validates the minimal-information framing——more information (token probs) doesn't necessarily help when the contamination mechanism is SFT-style.\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 Min-K%++ 在 SFT contamination 上 AUROC=0.61——高于 random 但远低于 lz* 的 model-level detection (d=3.4)。SFT 确实在 token-level 留下微弱信号（seen items 的 perplexity 略低），但 QLoRA 的 low-rank constraint 限制了 memorization 精度——模型学到的是 \\\"pattern-level\\\" 而非 \\\"token-level\\\" 的记忆，导致 Min-K%++ 这种依赖 token-level anomaly 的 方法效果有限。这与 MIA-loss 类似 (AUROC=0.59)——两者本质上测量同一信号 (token probability anomaly) 的不同 summary。Base model (未 SFT) 上两者 ~random (0.49) 因为没有 memorization 信号。Post-RL 时 AUROC 回到 ~0.51 (near random)——RL 的 distributional shift 完全掩盖了残余的 token-level signal，与 Wang et al. (2025) 一致。\\n\"\n898\t  },\n899\t  {\n900\t    \"name\": \"ARC-C Benchmark Validation (Small Benchmark)\",\n901\t    \"description\": \"ARC-Challenge (295 items) 上的控制实验——验证 small benchmark 检测极限。\\n\",\n902\t    \"results\": {\n903\t      \"arcc_clean_lz\": -5.5,\n904\t      \"arcc_contam15_lz\": -4.9,\n905\t      \"arcc_contam50_lz\": -4.6,\n906\t      \"arcc_delta_lz_15\": 0.6,\n907\t      \"arcc_delta_lz_50\": 0.9,\n908\t      \"arcc_cohens_d_15_free\": -0.5,\n909\t      \"arcc_cohens_d_50_free\": -0.8,\n910\t      \"arcc_theta_fixed_d_15\": 0.8,\n911\t      \"arcc_theta_fixed_d_50\": 1.2,\n912\t      \"arcc_power_theory_15\": 0.129,\n913\t      \"arcc_memo_frac\": 0.3\n914\t    },\n915\t    \"tables\": [\n916\t      {\n917\t        \"name\": \"Table: ARC-C Detection (Small Benchmark Regime)\",\n918\t        \"columns\": [\n919\t          \"condition\",\n920\t          \"lz_star\",\n921\t          \"delta_lz\",\n922\t          \"d_free\",\n923\t          \"d_theta_fixed\"\n924\t        ],\n925\t        \"rows\": [\n926\t          [\n927\t            \"clean (mean)\",\n928\t            -5.5,\n929\t            0,\n930\t            \"-\",\n931\t            \"-\"\n932\t          ],\n933\t          [\n934\t            \"contam_15\",\n935\t            -4.9,\n936\t            0.6,\n937\t            -0.5,\n938\t            0.8\n939\t          ],\n940\t          [\n941\t            \"contam_50\",\n942\t            -4.6,\n943\t            0.9,\n944\t            -0.8,\n945\t            1.2\n946\t          ]\n947\t        ]\n948\t      }\n949\t    ],\n950\t    \"figures\": [],\n951\t    \"analysis\": \"ARC-C 结果验证 power theory 预测——小 benchmark 检测力弱是理论预期。 θ-fixed 部分补偿但不改变根本限制。论文中作为 Claim 2 的支撑证据—— detection power 与 n_items 的关系在实际数据中得到验证。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 ARC-C (295 items) 在 free-θ 下检测力很弱 (d ~0.5 at 15%) 因为 power theory 预测仅 12.9% power。295 items 的 lz* 方差大——noise floor 高导致 signal/noise ratio 低。θ-fixed 改善至 d ~0.8-1.2 因为消除了 θ-shift confound，但仍远低于 MMLU 的 d=3.4。Memorization fraction ~30% 意味着 15% contamination 仅 ~44 items 被记忆——在 295 items 中产生的 pattern distortion 不够大。这与 power theory 的 min_items_15pct_80power =7958 一致——ARC-C 远低于此阈值。θ-fixed analysis 的 arcc_theta_fixed_d 在 [0.5, 1.5] 范围内——detectable 但效应弱。这是一个\\\"honest characterization\\\" 而非限制——小 benchmark 的检测力弱是信息论预期。\\n\"\n952\t  },\n953\t  {\n954\t    \"name\": \"HT vs lz* Post-RL Differentiation\",\n955\t    \"description\": \"Post-RL 条件下 HT 与 lz* 的 differential robustness 测试。\\n\",\n956\t    \"results\": {\n957\t      \"lz_star_post_rl_d\": 1.5,\n958\t      \"ht_post_rl_d\": 1.3,\n959\t      \"lz_star_ht_ratio_post_rl\": 1.15,\n960\t      \"lz_star_ht_ratio_pre_rl\": 1.07,\n961\t      \"differentiation_significant\": false,\n962\t      \"differentiation_p_value\": 0.35\n963\t    },\n964\t    \"tables\": [\n965\t      {\n966\t        \"name\": \"Table: lz* vs HT Post-RL Comparison\",\n967\t        \"columns\": [\n968\t          \"statistic\",\n969\t          \"pre_rl_d\",\n970\t          \"post_rl_d\",\n971\t          \"retention\",\n972\t          \"ratio_lz_over_ht\"\n973\t        ],\n974\t        \"rows\": [\n975\t          [\n976\t            \"lz*\",\n977\t            -3.42,\n978\t            -1.5,\n979\t            \"44%\",\n980\t            \"-\"\n981\t          ],\n982\t          [\n983\t            \"HT\",\n984\t            -3.21,\n985\t            -1.3,\n986\t            \"40%\",\n987\t            \"-\"\n988\t          ],\n989\t          [\n990\t            \"ratio\",\n991\t            1.07,\n992\t            1.15,\n993\t            \"-\",\n994\t            \"n.s. (p=0.35)\"\n995\t          ]\n996\t        ]\n997\t      }\n998\t    ],\n999\t    \"figures\": [],\n1000\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档叙事应对（对应 R12 reviewer concern）：empirical differentiation 失败 → 激活数据无关差异化三论证：(i) parametric null N(0,1)——bootstrap 已验证 lz* null 分布 mean=0.09/std=1.00，HT 无此性质，需 per-case bootstrap； (ii) Snijders correction Var*=Var_l - C²/I(θ) 补偿 θ 估计误差——尤其在 θ-fixed 不可用时 (e.g., retrospective audit without clean baseline)； (iii) 4PL a-weighting 在 MMLU 57 subjects 高异质性下理论更精确——虽然 empirical d 差异不显著，但信息论上 lz* 使用了更多 item-level information。 论文应坦诚报告并将这些论证置于 Discussion §6。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心预期：lz* 和 HT post-RL 退化幅度相似，差异不显著 (p=0.35)。 ratio 从 pre-RL 1.07 微升至 1.15——lz* 略好但 n=1 (单一模型) 条件下无法 得出统计结论。原因：post-RL 的 signal degradation 作用于 response pattern level——RL 改变了模型对 items 的作答方式（从记忆转向推理），这一变化对所有 基于 response pattern 的统计量影响相似。lz* 的 4PL weighting 在 large n (14K items) 下的优势被 RL-induced noise 部分抵消。HT 的 robustness 来自其 simplicity——仅依赖 difficulty ordering，RL 对 difficulty ordering 的扰动 较小。结论：无法通过 post-RL 实验 empirically differentiate lz* vs HT—— 转用数据无关差异化策略。\\n\"\n1001\t  },\n1002\t  {\n1003\t    \"name\": \"Mistral n=1 Supporting Evidence\",\n1004\t    \"description\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 单 clean seed 控制实验——作为第三个 family 的 supporting evidence。\\n\",\n1005\t    \"results\": {\n1006\t      \"mistral_clean_lz\": 5.42,\n1007\t      \"mistral_contam15_lz\": -1.38,\n1008\t      \"mistral_contam50_lz\": -3.15,\n1009\t      \"mistral_delta_lz_15\": -6.8,\n1010\t      \"mistral_delta_lz_50\": -8.57,\n1011\t      \"mistral_acc_clean\": 0.514,\n1012\t      \"mistral_contam15_acc\": 0.595,\n1013\t      \"mistral_memo_frac_15\": 0.34,\n1014\t      \"mistral_n_clean_seeds\": 1,\n1015\t      \"mistral_cohens_d_estimate\": \"N/A (n=1, no variance estimate)\"\n1016\t    },\n1017\t    \"tables\": [\n1018\t      {\n1019\t        \"name\": \"Table: Mistral Supporting Evidence (n=1)\",\n1020\t        \"columns\": [\n1021\t          \"condition\",\n1022\t          \"lz_star\",\n1023\t          \"delta_lz\",\n1024\t          \"acc\",\n1025\t          \"theta\",\n1026\t          \"memo_frac\"\n1027\t        ],\n1028\t        \"rows\": [\n1029\t          [\n1030\t            \"clean\",\n1031\t            5.42,\n1032\t            0,\n1033\t            0.514,\n1034\t            -1.157,\n1035\t            \"-\"\n1036\t          ],\n1037\t          [\n1038\t            \"contam_15\",\n1039\t            -1.38,\n1040\t            -6.8,\n1041\t            0.595,\n1042\t            -0.713,\n1043\t            0.34\n1044\t          ],\n1045\t          [\n1046\t            \"contam_50\",\n1047\t            -3.15,\n1048\t            -8.57,\n1049\t            0.673,\n1050\t            -0.303,\n1051\t            0.29\n1052\t          ]\n1053\t        ]\n1054\t      }\n1055\t    ],\n1056\t    \"figures\": [],\n1057\t    \"analysis\": \"Supporting evidence。n=1 不支持独立 claim 但与 Qwen/Llama 一致的方向性 结果增强跨家族泛化叙事。注意 Mistral 的 Δlz* 绝对值更大反映的是低能力 模型的更强 contamination signal——与 power theory 一致（低 θ baseline → 更大 response pattern shift）。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档 Mistral 仅 n=1 clean seed——无法计算 Cohen's d 或 CI。但 Δlz*=-6.80 (15%) 的绝对值比 Qwen (-4.84) 和 Llama (-2.85) 更大，因为 Mistral 是最弱模型 (acc=0.514)——低能力模型受 contamination 的 response pattern distortion 更大（baseline 答错很多 items，contamination 后这些 items 突然答对，产生更极端的 aberrance）。Mistral baseline lz*=5.42 (正值) 意味着 clean model 已经 slightly over-consistent——contamination 后 lz* 翻转至负值 (-1.38) 说明 aberrance signal 足够强。作为 n=1 supporting evidence 而非 primary validation——论文中明确标注 \\\"single-seed, indicative\\\"。跨三个 family (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 的 detection success 足以支撑 n_families_validated=3。\\n\"\n1058\t  },\n1059\t  {\n1060\t    \"name\": \"Full Baseline Comparison Table (Frontier Ranking)\",\n1061\t    \"description\": \"Detection frontier 完整排名表——所有方法按信息访问层级排列。\\n\",\n1062\t    \"results\": {\n1063\t      \"n_baselines_total\": 7,\n1064\t      \"n_baselines_beaten_at_model_level\": 4,\n1065\t      \"frontier_ranking\": {\n1066\t        \"binary_only\": [\n1067\t          \"Guttman (d=0.43)\",\n1068\t          \"U3 (d=0.38)\",\n1069\t          \"random (d=0)\"\n1070\t        ],\n1071\t        \"binary_plus_difficulty\": [\n1072\t          \"HT (d=3.21)\"\n1073\t        ],\n1074\t        \"binary_plus_4pl\": [\n1075\t          \"lz* (d=3.42)\"\n1076\t        ],\n1077\t        \"binary_plus_retest\": [\n1078\t          \"ConStat (AUROC=0.78)\"\n1079\t        ],\n1080\t        \"token_probs\": [\n1081\t          \"Min-K%++ (AUROC=0.61)\",\n1082\t          \"MIA-loss (AUROC=0.59)\"\n1083\t        ]\n1084\t      },\n1085\t      \"key_comparison\": \"person-fit family (HT + lz*) >> pure binary (Guttman/U3) >> token-prob (Min-K++)\"\n1086\t    },\n1087\t    \"tables\": [\n1088\t      {\n1089\t        \"name\": \"Table: Detection Frontier Ranking\",\n1090\t        \"columns\": [\n1091\t          \"method\",\n1092\t          \"info_access\",\n1093\t          \"model_d_or_auroc\",\n1094\t          \"item_auroc\",\n1095\t          \"extra_cost\",\n1096\t          \"interpretable\"\n1097\t        ],\n1098\t        \"rows\": [\n1099\t          [\n1100\t            \"lz* (ours)\",\n1101\t            \"binary + 4PL params\",\n1102\t            \"d=-3.42\",\n1103\t            0.536,\n1104\t            \"0 (calibrated params available)\",\n1105\t            \"Yes\"\n1106\t          ],\n1107\t          [\n1108\t            \"HT\",\n1109\t            \"binary + difficulty\",\n1110\t            \"d=-3.21\",\n1111\t            \"N/A\",\n1112\t            0,\n1113\t            \"Limited\"\n1114\t          ],\n1115\t          [\n1116\t            \"acc z-score\",\n1117\t            \"binary + pop stats\",\n1118\t            \"z=160.6\",\n1119\t            \"N/A\",\n1120\t            0,\n1121\t            \"No (no specificity)\"\n1122\t          ],\n1123\t          [\n1124\t            \"ConStat\",\n1125\t            \"binary + retest\",\n1126\t            \"AUROC=0.78\",\n1127\t            \"N/A\",\n1128\t            \"3× inference\",\n1129\t            \"Partial\"\n1130\t          ],\n1131\t          [\n1132\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n1133\t            \"token probs\",\n1134\t            \"AUROC=0.61\",\n1135\t            \"N/A\",\n1136\t            \"API access\",\n1137\t            \"No\"\n1138\t          ],\n1139\t          [\n1140\t            \"MIA-loss\",\n1141\t            \"token probs\",\n1142\t            \"AUROC=0.59\",\n1143\t            \"N/A\",\n1144\t            \"API access\",\n1145\t            \"No\"\n1146\t          ],\n1147\t          [\n1148\t            \"Guttman/U3\",\n1149\t            \"binary only\",\n1150\t            \"d=-0.43\",\n1151\t            \"N/A\",\n1152\t            0,\n1153\t            \"No\"\n1154\t          ],\n1155\t          [\n1156\t            \"random\",\n1157\t            \"none\",\n1158\t            \"d=0\",\n1159\t            0.5,\n1160\t            0,\n1161\t            \"No\"\n1162\t          ]\n1163\t        ]\n1164\t      }\n1165\t    ],\n1166\t    \"figures\": [],\n1167\t    \"analysis\": \"n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT tied。ConStat effective but higher info cost。Acc z-score 不 comparable (no specificity)。 Total ≥5 baselines 满足同行中位数要求。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档 frontier ranking 清晰呈现信息层级与检测力的关系：(1) 纯 binary (Guttman/U3) 最弱因为不利用 item difficulty 信息——仅看 response pattern 的 non-randomness，无法区分 high-ability 与 contamination；(2) binary + difficulty (HT) 跳跃式提升至 d=3.21——difficulty ordering 是关键信息， 让统计量能识别 \\\"答对不该答对的题\\\"；(3) binary + 4PL (lz*) 在 HT 基础上 marginal gain——a/c/d 参数的额外信息在 14K items 下被 averaging 稀释； (4) token-prob methods 反而弱于 binary person-fit——说明 \\\"更多信息\\\" 不等于 \\\"更好检测\\\"，信息类型比信息量重要。SFT contamination 的 token-level signal 很弱 (memorization fraction ~35%)，而 response-pattern-level signal 通过 14K items 聚合后很强。这是论文的核心 insight 之一。\\n\"\n1168\t  },\n1169\t  {\n1170\t    \"name\": \"Gemma-4-31B Controlled Contamination (Conditional)\",\n1171\t    \"description\": \"Gemma-4-31B 控制实验——第四个 family，median 档下可能部分失败。\\n\",\n1172\t    \"results\": {\n1173\t      \"gemma_training_stable\": \"uncertain\",\n1174\t      \"gemma_qlora_rank\": 64,\n1175\t      \"gemma_gpu_hours\": 20,\n1176\t      \"gemma_clean_lz\": 3.2,\n1177\t      \"gemma_contam15_d\": -2.2,\n1178\t      \"gemma_contam50_d\": -2.8,\n1179\t      \"gemma_partial_failure_risk\": 0.35,\n1180\t      \"gemma_memo_frac\": 0.32,\n1181\t      \"fallback\": \"drop to 3 families if training unstable\"\n1182\t    },\n1183\t    \"tables\": [\n1184\t      {\n1185\t        \"name\": \"Table: Gemma Conditional Results\",\n1186\t        \"columns\": [\n1187\t          \"condition\",\n1188\t          \"lz_star\",\n1189\t          \"delta_lz\",\n1190\t          \"d_estimate\",\n1191\t          \"training_status\"\n1192\t        ],\n1193\t        \"rows\": [\n1194\t          [\n1195\t            \"clean\",\n1196\t            3.2,\n1197\t            0,\n1198\t            \"-\",\n1199\t            \"stable\"\n1200\t          ],\n1201\t          [\n1202\t            \"contam_15\",\n1203\t            \"~0.5\",\n1204\t            \"-2.7\",\n1205\t            -2.2,\n1206\t            \"stable/unstable\"\n1207\t          ],\n1208\t          [\n1209\t            \"contam_50\",\n1210\t            \"~-0.8\",\n1211\t            \"-4.0\",\n1212\t            -2.8,\n1213\t            \"stable/unstable\"\n1214\t          ]\n1215\t        ]\n1216\t      }\n1217\t    ],\n1218\t    \"figures\": [],\n1219\t    \"analysis\": \"Conditional on training stability。如果成功 → n_families_validated=4 (bonus)。如果失败 → 3 families 已足够，Gemma 的 scale difference (31B vs 7-9B) 写入 Limitations 作为 future work。\\n\\nMedian 档 Gemma-4-31B 是最不确定的实验。31B 参数量显著大于其他三个 (7-9B)， QLoRA 行为可能不同：(1) rank=64 的 low-rank adaptation 在 31B 模型上 adaptation 比例更小——可能需要更多 epochs 或更高 rank；(2) Gemma 架构 (Google) 与 Qwen/Llama/Mistral 不同——可能有不同的 SFT 泛化特性； (3) 训练不稳定风险 ~35%（loss divergence or poor convergence）。如果成功， d ~2.2-2.8 处于可接受范围。如果部分失败（如某些 contamination levels 不收敛）， 降级为 footnote evidence。3 families (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 已足够支撑 cross-family claim——Gemma 是 bonus。Memorization fraction 可能略低 (0.32) 因为大模型 QLoRA 的 effective capacity 更分散。\\n\"\n1220\t  }\n1221\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea1e9cd0-76ef-4277-8837-49ffa06069a9","uuid":"d78528b8-da65-40f7-85fd-493c70776053","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:55:59.424Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122444/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Controlled Contamination Pilot (Qwen)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B × 4 conditions (0%-seed1/0%-seed2/15%/50%) × MMLU only. Go/no-go 信号实验。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"clean_seed1_lz_star\": 8.5,\n      \"clean_seed2_lz_star\": 7.9,\n      \"clean_mean\": 8.2,\n      \"clean_std\": 0.42,\n      \"contam_15_lz_star\": 4.1,\n      \"contam_50_lz_star\": 7.0,\n      \"delta_lz_star_15\": -4.1,\n      \"delta_lz_star_50\": -1.2,\n      \"cohens_d_contam15\": -3.2,\n      \"cohens_d_contam50\": -1.1,\n      \"contam_15_acc\": 0.72,\n      \"contam_50_acc\": 0.76,\n      \"memorization_fraction_15\": 0.36,\n      \"memorization_fraction_50\": 0.28,\n      \"seen_lz_star_15\": 0.3,\n      \"unseen_lz_star_15\": 3.2,\n      \"theta_shift_15\": 0.25,\n      \"theta_shift_50\": 0.45,\n      \"theta_fixed_contam15_lz\": 11.5,\n      \"theta_fixed_contam50_lz\": 17.8,\n      \"theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.9\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen Pilot Controlled Contamination Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"delta_lz_star\",\n          \"cohens_d\",\n          \"acc\",\n          \"theta_mle\",\n          \"lz_star_fixed\",\n          \"memo_frac\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"clean_s1\",\n            8.5,\n            0,\n            \"-\",\n            0.678,\n            -0.1,\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean_s2\",\n            7.9,\n            0,\n            \"-\",\n            0.676,\n            -0.11,\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_15\",\n            4.1,\n            -4.1,\n            -3.2,\n            0.72,\n            0.15,\n            11.5,\n            0.36\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_50\",\n            7.0,\n            -1.2,\n            -1.1,\n            0.76,\n            0.35,\n            17.8,\n            0.28\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Go 信号确认。|d|>2 at 15% 足以支撑 Claim 1。Non-monotonicity 在 free-θ 下出现 是预期的，θ-fixed 恢复单调性是方法论贡献。Memorization fraction ~36% 与 SFT generalization 一致——QLoRA 仅记忆约 1/3 注入 items，其余通过泛化提升。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 Qwen 控制实验预期产生强效应但 free-θ 下 50% contamination 出现 non-monotonicity。Qwen baseline lz* 高 (~8-9) 因其 response pattern 与 4PL 预测高度一致但非完美匹配；15% 污染产生明显 aberrance（memorization fraction ~36% 意味着约 1/3 seen items 被记忆，产生 difficulty-inconsistent correct responses）。 50% 条件下 θ-shift 吸收大量 aberrance 信号导致 free-θ d 值下降至 ~1.1，但 θ-fixed 恢复单调性（ratio ~2.9）。这与 Qwen 高 baseline misfit (lz*~8.5) 交互——高 baseline 模型更容易出现 non-monotonicity 因为 θ 估计对 response pattern 变化更敏感。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Controlled Contamination (4 Families)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B + Gemma-4-31B + Llama-3.1-8B + Mistral-7B-v0.3 × 6 levels (0/5/10/15/25/50%) × MMLU + GSM8K + HellaSwag。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_families_validated\": 3,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_d15\": -3.4,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_d50\": -1.0,\n      \"llama_mmlu_d15\": -2.9,\n      \"llama_mmlu_d50\": -3.3,\n      \"mistral_mmlu_d15\": -2.5,\n      \"mistral_mmlu_d50\": -3.0,\n      \"gemma_mmlu_d15\": -2.2,\n      \"gemma_mmlu_d50\": -2.8,\n      \"gemma_note\": \"Gemma 31B 参数量大，QLoRA 效率不同，可能需调参或 drop\",\n      \"gsm8k_avg_d15\": -1.5,\n      \"gsm8k_avg_d50\": -2.0,\n      \"hellaswag_avg_d15\": -1.8,\n      \"hellaswag_avg_d50\": -2.5,\n      \"cross_family_memo_frac_range\": [\n        0.3,\n        0.4\n      ],\n      \"cross_family_memo_frac_mean\": 0.35,\n      \"dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed\": true,\n      \"dose_response_monotonic_free\": \"model-dependent\",\n      \"n_conditions_total\": 72,\n      \"n_conditions_significant\": 55,\n      \"small_benchmark_weakness\": \"GSM8K (1319 items) d ~1.5 at 15%, below MMLU\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Family Detection Summary (MMLU, θ-free)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"family\",\n          \"clean_lz\",\n          \"d_5pct\",\n          \"d_10pct\",\n          \"d_15pct\",\n          \"d_25pct\",\n          \"d_50pct\",\n          \"memo_frac_15\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen-7B\",\n            8.7,\n            -0.8,\n            -1.8,\n            -3.4,\n            -2.8,\n            -1.0,\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-8B\",\n            -0.1,\n            -0.5,\n            -1.5,\n            -2.9,\n            -3.1,\n            -3.3,\n            0.35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B\",\n            5.4,\n            -0.7,\n            -1.6,\n            -2.5,\n            -2.8,\n            -3.0,\n            0.34\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-31B\",\n            3.2,\n            -0.4,\n            -1.0,\n            -2.2,\n            -2.5,\n            -2.8,\n            0.32\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Benchmark Detection (15% contamination, all families avg)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"avg_d\",\n          \"power_theory\",\n          \"memo_frac\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            -2.8,\n            0.979,\n            0.35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            -1.8,\n            0.753,\n            0.33\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            -1.5,\n            0.591,\n            0.3\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"3 families 足以支撑跨家族泛化 claim。Gemma 若部分失败，以 footnote 说明参数量/ QLoRA 差异。n_items 效应与 power theory 一致——这本身强化 Claim 2。Memorization fraction 跨家族一致性 (3pp 差异) 是关键发现，支撑 SFT 泛化机制的普适性。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 3/4 families 成功验证（n_families_validated=3）。Gemma-4-31B 因 参数量大且 QLoRA rank 可能不足，存在训练不稳定或效果弱化风险——median 档下 Gemma 可能仅提供 partial 结果或需 downgrade 为 supporting evidence。跨 benchmark 差异反映 n_items 效应（MMLU 14042 >> GSM8K 1319）——power theory 预测 GSM8K 在 15% 仅有 ~59% power，对应 d ~1.5。HellaSwag (10042 items) 介于两者 之间。Memorization fraction 跨家族一致 (~35%) 是 SFT 机制的稳定性质， 不依赖模型架构——QLoRA 的泛化模式相似因为都是 low-rank adaptation。Free-θ non-monotonicity 仅出现在高 baseline lz* 模型（Qwen, Mistral），Llama (baseline ~0) 保持单调。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Audit (ABANDONED)\",\n    \"description\": \"Open LLM Leaderboard v1 大规模扫描。已因 MML-EM refit 失败 (a_r=0.111) 而放弃。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"ABANDONED\",\n      \"reason\": \"a_r=0.111 discrimination failure makes v1-refit IRT parameters unreliable\",\n      \"data_availability_noted\": true,\n      \"n_models_available\": \"13000+\",\n      \"future_work_mention\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"放弃是正确决定。论文中将 refit 失败作为 methodological caveat (Claim 3c) 展示——量化经典 IRT 与 neural IRT 估计的 sample size gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下此实验不执行。MML-EM 从 N=63→178 模型重拟合 IRT 参数，discrimination 参数 a_r=0.111 远低于 0.2 阈值——经典 IRT 拟合方法在 LLM 数据上失效因为： (1) 样本量仍不足（经典 IRT 需 N>500），(2) LLM response pattern 违反 local independence（同 domain items 相关），(3) 模型能力分布与 IRT 假设不匹配。 13K+ 数据可用性写入 Discussion/Future Work 作为 scaling roadmap。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Natural Experiment (v1 base→chat pairs)\",\n    \"description\": \"v1 leaderboard base→chat model pairs 的 Δlz* 作为 SFT 效应代理。P2-optional。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_pairs\": 21,\n      \"n_complete_pairs\": 9,\n      \"significant_benchmarks\": 2,\n      \"hellaswag_mean_deviation\": -3.4,\n      \"hellaswag_p\": 0.001,\n      \"gsm8k_mean_deviation\": 3.9,\n      \"gsm8k_p\": 0.009,\n      \"mmlu_p\": 0.15,\n      \"arcc_p\": 0.38,\n      \"individual_outliers\": 0,\n      \"interpretation\": \"systematic SFT effects, not contamination-specific\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Natural Experiment SFT Effects\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"mean_delta_lz\",\n          \"t_stat\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            -3.4,\n            -3.97,\n            0.001,\n            \"SFT decreases person-fit\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            3.9,\n            3.35,\n            0.009,\n            \"SFT increases person-fit\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"+1.2\",\n            1.54,\n            0.15,\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            \"-0.8\",\n            -0.91,\n            0.38,\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Supplementary evidence only。系统性 SFT 方向差异 (HellaSwag↓, GSM8K↑) 有趣 但因 refit 参数质量问题不做强 claim。P2 降级合理。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 显示系统性 SFT 效应（方向一致的 Δlz* shift） 但无个体 pair 出现 benchmark-specific 异常。这是因为 chat 模型的 SFT 训练 普遍改变了 response pattern——HellaSwag (commonsense) 受 instruction tuning 负面影响（降低 person-fit），GSM8K (math) 受益（提高 person-fit）。但用 a_r=0.111 的 refit 参数计算的 lz* 本质上退化为 accuracy-like 指标，无法 区分 contamination 与 legitimate SFT improvement。仅 9 个 complete pairs 缺乏统计检验力做细粒度分析。作为 P2 supplementary evidence 足够。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"v1 IRT Refit Expanded (N≥500)\",\n    \"description\": \"扩大 v1 IRT 重拟合样本量至 N≥500，最终关闭 Path D。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_downloaded\": 178,\n      \"a_pearson_r_3pl\": 0.127,\n      \"a_pearson_r_2pl\": -0.029,\n      \"b_pearson_r_3pl\": 0.663,\n      \"conclusion\": \"Path D dead — discrimination failure persists at N=178\",\n      \"threshold_met\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: IRT Refit Parameter Recovery\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"n_models\",\n          \"a_r\",\n          \"b_r\",\n          \"conclusion\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"3PL pilot\",\n            63,\n            0.111,\n            0.626,\n            \"dead\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3PL expanded\",\n            178,\n            0.127,\n            0.663,\n            \"dead\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2PL expanded\",\n            178,\n            -0.029,\n            0.572,\n            \"dead\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Path D 最终关闭。论文 Claim 3c 中作为 methodological caveat 展示。 关键贡献：量化经典 IRT 与 LLM context 的 sample size gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 N=178 仍无法恢复 discrimination 参数（a_r=0.127, 远低于 0.4 可行阈值）。根本原因不是样本量而是经典 MML-EM 拟合方法的结构性限制： (1) LLM response pattern 不满足 local independence——同 domain 1000+ items 高度相关，(2) 能力维度 θ 对 LLM 而言不是单一维度——不同 benchmark 需要不同 \\\"能力\\\"，(3) N=178 模型虽多于 pilot 的 63，但 item 数 14042 远超模型数， 导致 over-determined 系统。b_r=0.663 部分成功因为 difficulty 与 accuracy 线性相关——即使模型不多也能恢复。a (discrimination) 需要建模 item 间差异化 响应概率的曲率，这需要更多分布覆盖。Path D 确认关闭。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"4PL vs 3PL Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"4PL vs 3PL(d=1) ablation——量化 feasibility parameter d 对检测的影响。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"far_4pl\": 0.05,\n      \"far_3pl\": \"4.7-16.5%\",\n      \"far_2pl\": \"50-100%\",\n      \"mean_power_gain_mmlu\": \"+27pp\",\n      \"mean_power_gain_hellaswag\": \"+26pp\",\n      \"mean_power_gain_gsm8k\": \"+20pp\",\n      \"items_with_d_lt_0.95_mmlu\": \"46%\",\n      \"max_power_gain\": \"+59pp (HellaSwag)\",\n      \"deepseek_v3_delta\": 357\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Power (25% contamination)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"power_4pl\",\n          \"power_3pl\",\n          \"gain\",\n          \"pct_items_d_lt_0.95\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.776,\n            0.329,\n            \"+44.7pp\",\n            \"46%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.534,\n            0.28,\n            \"+25.4pp\",\n            \"38%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.73,\n            0.334,\n            \"+39.6pp\",\n            \"42%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            0.132,\n            0.091,\n            \"+4.1pp\",\n            \"28%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.318,\n            0.165,\n            \"+15.3pp\",\n            \"35%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"4PL 对 LLM 应用必要性的强证据。回应 R8 reviewer concern。结论：使用 3PL 会丢失约一半检测力。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 4PL d 参数对检测至关重要。46% MMLU items 有 d<0.95——这些 items 的 upper asymptote 低于 1.0，意味着即使能力极高的模型也无法以 100% 概率答对。 忽略 d (设 d=1) 使得 4PL 模型对高能力模型的预测概率系统性偏高，产生虚假 aberrance 信号——高能力模型答错一个 d=0.8 的 item 是正常的，但 3PL 认为是 异常。结果：(1) 3PL FAR 膨胀至 4.7-16.5%（benchmark 依赖），(2) detection power 平均下降 20-27pp 因为 noise floor 升高，(3) 2PL 更灾难性（FAR 50-100%） 因为同时忽略了 guessing parameter c。power gain 在 d<0.8 bucket 最大 (+6.8 to +61.2pp)，d≥0.95 时 gain 可忽略。这证明 PSN-IRT 的 4PL 参数化对 LLM contamination detection 而非 academic nicety 是必要的。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison (≥5 baselines)\",\n    \"description\": \"在控制实验 ground-truth contaminated models 上比较 IRT-FIT vs ≥5 baselines。 包括 ConStat (retest), Min-K%++ (token probs), acc z-score, HT, Guttman/U3。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model_level_lz_star_d_qwen15\": -3.42,\n      \"model_level_ht_d_qwen15\": -3.21,\n      \"model_level_guttman_d_qwen15\": -0.43,\n      \"model_level_u3_d_qwen15\": -0.38,\n      \"model_level_acc_zscore\": 160.6,\n      \"ht_vs_lz_star_ratio\": 0.94,\n      \"lz_star_vs_guttman_ratio\": 8.0,\n      \"constat_retest_auroc\": 0.78,\n      \"mink_sft_auroc\": 0.6,\n      \"item_level_max_auroc\": 0.63,\n      \"item_level_lz_itemwise_auroc\": 0.536,\n      \"item_level_irt_residual_auroc\": 0.582,\n      \"item_level_lr_cross_auroc\": 0.592,\n      \"item_level_rf_oracle_auroc\": 0.63,\n      \"n_baselines_beaten\": 4,\n      \"n_baselines_total\": 6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Model-Level Baseline Comparison (Qwen 15% contamination)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"info_required\",\n          \"cohens_d\",\n          \"requires_retest\",\n          \"interpretable\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz* (ours)\",\n            \"binary + 4PL params\",\n            -3.42,\n            \"No\",\n            \"Yes (θ-shift, memo frac)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HT\",\n            \"binary + item difficulty\",\n            -3.21,\n            \"No\",\n            \"Limited\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Guttman\",\n            \"binary only\",\n            -0.43,\n            \"No\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"U3\",\n            \"binary only\",\n            -0.38,\n            \"No\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"acc z-score\",\n            \"binary + population stats\",\n            -160.6,\n            \"No\",\n            \"No (specificity issue)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            \"binary + retest\",\n            \"AUROC=0.78\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"Partial\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            \"token probabilities\",\n            \"AUROC=0.60\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Item-Level Detection (all methods near-random)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"auroc_qwen15\",\n          \"auroc_qwen50\",\n          \"auroc_llama15\",\n          \"auroc_llama50\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz_itemwise\",\n            0.536,\n            0.535,\n            0.528,\n            0.536\n          ],\n          [\n            \"irt_residual\",\n            0.578,\n            0.563,\n            0.582,\n            0.581\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lr_cross_model\",\n            0.586,\n            0.567,\n            0.592,\n            0.585\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rf_oracle\",\n            0.61,\n            0.63,\n            0.615,\n            0.629\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random\",\n            0.5,\n            0.5,\n            0.5,\n            0.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档叙事转向：lz* 的优势不在 raw detection power（HT comparable）而在 interpretability 和 framework contribution。n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT comparable 但缺乏 parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting——这些在 MMLU 57 subjects 异质性大时理论上更精确。 ConStat 有效但需 retest (更多信息)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心发现：HT 与 lz* 在 model-level detection 上差距很小 (d ratio ~0.94)——HT 仅需 item difficulty，无需完整 4PL 参数化，却达到 comparable 效果。这是因为 model-level aggregation 对 14K items 的 central limit theorem 效应使得 item-level 参数权重差异被平均掉——HT 的 uniform weighting 与 lz* 的 a-weighted 方案在大 n 下收敛。lz* vs Guttman/U3 的 8× 差距证明 IRT 框架（含 difficulty ordering）优于纯 response pattern 统计。 ConStat retest AUROC=0.78 有效但需额外推理轮次（更多信息），符合 detection frontier 叙事。Min-K%++ 在 SFT 上 AUROC=0.60（弱），因为 SFT 改变了 token 分布但未产生 memorization-specific 的 perplexity 异常——SFT 后模型对 contaminated items 的 logprob 分布与 generalization 难以区分。Item-level 所有方法 near-random (max 0.63 with oracle) 因为 memorization fraction ~35% 意味着仅 1/3 items 产生可检测信号——这种 diffuse signature 只能通过 model-level aggregation 检测。acc z-score 的 z=160 说明它在 controlled setting 下 trivially 有效但无法在 real-world 中区分 contamination 与 legitimate high ability。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multiscale lzm Aggregation\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合的 标准化 lz* 总分。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lzm_gemini15\": 45.2,\n      \"lzm_deepseek_v3\": 38.7,\n      \"lzm_qwen_plus\": 35.1,\n      \"lzm_doubao\": -18.3,\n      \"lzm_mistral\": 12.4,\n      \"lzm_correlation_with_max_lz\": 0.92,\n      \"lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_clean\": 12.8,\n      \"lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_15\": 6.5,\n      \"lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_50\": 9.2,\n      \"added_value_over_per_benchmark\": \"marginal\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: lzm vs max-benchmark lz* (PSN-IRT 12 models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"lzm\",\n          \"max_lz_star\",\n          \"dominant_benchmark\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Gemini-1.5\",\n            45.2,\n            31.8,\n            \"MMLU\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-V3\",\n            38.7,\n            25.3,\n            \"MMLU\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen-Plus\",\n            35.1,\n            24.5,\n            \"MMLU\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Doubao-Pro\",\n            -18.3,\n            -15.2,\n            \"HellaSwag\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix material。lzm 在当前数据条件下不改变结论。未来若覆盖更多 benchmarks 且有 cross-benchmark differential contamination，lzm 可显示独立价值。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 lzm 提供 per-model 的单一污染严重度指标，但 added value 有限。 lzm 本质是各 benchmark lz* 的 variance-weighted sum——由于 MMLU lz* 已经 dominate (n=14042 产生最极端值)，lzm 高度相关于 max per-benchmark lz* (r=0.92)。在 PSN-IRT 12-model data 上，lzm 重现已知排序（Gemini-1.5 最高）。 在 ctrl-contam 上，因为只有 MMLU 数据，lzm 退化为 lz* itself。理论贡献： 展示 Hong et al. 公式对 LLM multi-benchmark 评估的适用性。但 median 档下 不产生 new insight——P2 优先级合理。若 full ctrl-contam 覆盖 3 benchmarks， lzm 可显示跨 benchmark aggregation 的 marginal gain。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Post-RL Hypothesis Test\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B 先 SFT 污染再 GRPO 训练，测试 person-fit 是否在 RL 后保持检测力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"post_rl_lz_star_cohens_d\": 1.5,\n      \"post_rl_ht_cohens_d\": 1.3,\n      \"post_rl_mia_auroc\": 0.52,\n      \"post_rl_mink_auroc\": 0.51,\n      \"pre_rl_lz_star_d\": -3.42,\n      \"signal_retention_lz\": 0.44,\n      \"signal_retention_ht\": 0.4,\n      \"rl_steps\": 2000,\n      \"reward_type\": \"rule-based (accuracy on held-out)\",\n      \"delta_lz_pre_rl\": -4.84,\n      \"delta_lz_post_rl\": -2.1,\n      \"delta_ht_post_rl\": -1.8,\n      \"theta_shift_post_rl\": 0.35,\n      \"acc_post_rl\": 0.74,\n      \"acc_seen_post_rl\": 0.7,\n      \"acc_unseen_post_rl\": 0.68,\n      \"memo_frac_post_rl\": 0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Post-RL Detection Power Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"pre_rl_d\",\n          \"post_rl_d\",\n          \"retention\",\n          \"info_level\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz*\",\n            -3.42,\n            -1.5,\n            \"44%\",\n            \"binary + 4PL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HT\",\n            -3.21,\n            -1.3,\n            \"40%\",\n            \"binary + difficulty\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Guttman\",\n            -0.43,\n            -0.2,\n            \"47%\",\n            \"binary only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            \"AUROC=0.60\",\n            \"AUROC=0.51\",\n            \"~random\",\n            \"token probs\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MIA-loss\",\n            \"AUROC=0.59\",\n            \"AUROC=0.52\",\n            \"~random\",\n            \"token probs\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Memorization Fraction Degradation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"stage\",\n          \"memo_frac\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"delta_lz\",\n          \"cohens_d\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            \"-\",\n            8.68,\n            0,\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"post-SFT (15%)\",\n            0.38,\n            3.85,\n            -4.84,\n            -3.42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"post-RL\",\n            0.12,\n            6.58,\n            -2.1,\n            -1.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档叙事策略：(1) person-fit FAMILY 在 post-RL 保留 detectable signal (d>1.0)，log-prob 方法完全失效——class-level advantage 确认；(2) lz* 与 HT 退化幅度相似，无法 empirically differentiate——转用数据无关差异化论证 (parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting)；(3) memorization fraction 从 38%→12% 量化了 RL 的 \\\"washing\\\" 效应——这本身是对 RL alignment 文献的贡献（RL 部分消除 SFT contamination）；(4) 论文 claim 从 \\\"lz* uniquely robust\\\" 软化为 \\\"person-fit family robust; lz* uniquely interpretable\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：post-RL signal partially degrades for ALL person-fit methods。 GRPO 优化使模型学会\\\"推理\\\"而非\\\"记忆\\\"——RL 的 reward signal 鼓励 generalizable reasoning patterns，这部分平滑了 SFT 注入的 memorization fingerprint。 具体机制：(1) memorization fraction 从 ~38% 降至 ~12%——RL 使模型对 seen items 的回答方式从 rote recall 转向 reasoning-based，部分 items 不再产生 difficulty-inconsistent response；(2) θ 进一步上升（RL 提升整体能力），吸收 更多 aberrance；(3) 但 ~12% items 仍保留 memorization signature——这些是 factual knowledge items 无法通过推理路径解答，只能靠记忆。lz* d=1.5 和 HT d=1.3 均在 [1.0, 2.0] 范围内——detectable 但 effect size 明显弱于 pre-RL。 两者退化幅度相似（signal_retention ~40-44%），说明 RL-induced degradation 作用于 response pattern level（person-fit 家族共享），非统计量特异性。MIA/ Min-K++ AUROC ~0.51-0.52（near random）符合 Wang et al. 发现——log-prob 方法在 RL 后完全失效，而 person-fit 保留 partial signal。这是 person-fit 作为 family 的 structural advantage，但无法 differentiate lz* vs HT。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extra Benchmarks (BBH + MATH)\",\n    \"description\": \"扩展 benchmark 覆盖：BBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 填充 1K-10K items 的 power gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bbh_4pl_available\": false,\n      \"math_4pl_available\": false,\n      \"bbh_2pl_refit_attempted\": true,\n      \"bbh_a_r\": 0.15,\n      \"math_a_r\": 0.12,\n      \"bbh_power_15pct_sim\": 0.68,\n      \"math_power_15pct_sim\": 0.62,\n      \"bbh_ctrl_contam_d15\": -1.8,\n      \"math_ctrl_contam_d15\": -1.2,\n      \"power_gap_filled\": \"partial\",\n      \"n_items_range_covered\": \"1319 (GSM8K) → 6511 (BBH) → 10042 (HellaSwag) → 14042 (MMLU)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Power Function Validation Across Benchmark Sizes\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"power_theory_15pct\",\n          \"power_sim_15pct\",\n          \"power_ctrl_d15\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            295,\n            0.129,\n            0.129,\n            \"0.5-1.5 (θ-fixed)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            0.591,\n            0.591,\n            \"-1.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MATH\",\n            5000,\n            0.62,\n            \"~0.62 (sim)\",\n            \"-1.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BBH\",\n            6511,\n            0.68,\n            \"~0.68 (sim)\",\n            \"-1.8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.753,\n            0.753,\n            \"-1.8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            0.979,\n            0.979,\n            \"-3.4\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Partial contribution。Power theory 插值验证有效但缺乏 PSN-IRT 级别的 4PL ground truth。若 PSN-IRT authors 有 BBH/MATH 参数可协作获取——否则仅报告 simulation-based 预测。P2 优先级合理——非论文核心但强化 Claim 2。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 PSN-IRT 不包含 BBH/MATH 的 4PL 参数——需自行拟合。但自行 拟合面临与 v1-refit 相同的问题：discrimination recovery 弱 (a_r ~0.12-0.15)。 Workaround：(1) 仅用 simulation（假设合理 4PL 参数分布）预测 power—— BBH 6511 items 在 15% 时 power ~68%（power theory R²=0.957 插值）， MATH 5000 items ~62%；(2) 如果有 ctrl-contam 数据，用 PSN-IRT MMLU 参数 的 distributional statistics 生成 synthetic 4PL 参数估计。Ctrl-contam 实际 d 值偏低 (BBH d ~1.8, MATH d ~1.2) 因为拟合参数质量不如 PSN-IRT——但仍 在 detectable 范围。填充 power gap 是 partial 的：power theory 插值有效， 但缺乏 ground-truth 4PL 参数的直接验证。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Domain-Level Analysis (MMLU subjects)\",\n    \"description\": \"按 MMLU subject category 分别计算 person-fit，识别污染的 domain 分布模式。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gemini_accuracy\": 1.0,\n      \"gemini_subjects_flagged\": \"50/57\",\n      \"gemini_domain_concentrated\": false,\n      \"gemini_stem_lz\": 21.2,\n      \"gemini_humanities_lz\": 17.9,\n      \"gemini_social_sciences_lz\": 15.9,\n      \"gemini_other_lz\": 15.3,\n      \"doubao_negative_lz\": true,\n      \"doubao_stem_lz\": -2.0,\n      \"doubao_humanities_lz\": -13.0,\n      \"doubao_social_sciences_lz\": -14.8,\n      \"ctrl_contam_domain_uniform\": true,\n      \"ctrl_contam_seen_unseen_per_domain\": \"consistent across domains\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Domain-Level lz* Profile (Selected Models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"STEM\",\n          \"Humanities\",\n          \"Social_Sci\",\n          \"Other\",\n          \"pattern\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Gemini-1.5\",\n            21.2,\n            17.9,\n            15.9,\n            15.3,\n            \"uniform high\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Doubao-Pro\",\n            -2.0,\n            -13.0,\n            -14.8,\n            4.4,\n            \"selective negative\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Hunyuan-Large\",\n            1.8,\n            8.5,\n            13.9,\n            6.2,\n            \"social science high\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Yi-Lightning\",\n            48.2,\n            35.1,\n            42.5,\n            38.9,\n            \"uniform extreme\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix or §5.3 subsection。Domain-level 分析支撑 Claim 3b (anomaly profiles)。Selective vs uniform 模式为 contamination typology 提供 mechanistic insight。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 domain analysis 确认两种 contamination 模式：(1) Gemini-1.5 的 uniform 高 lz* 横跨 50/57 subjects——全面 contamination 或极高能力 (acc=100%)，无法区分但 domain 均匀性本身是 pattern；(2) Doubao 的 selective negative lz*——Humanities/Social Sciences 显示强 negative aberrance (lz* -13 to -15)，暗示这些 domains 的 training data 与 MMLU item distribution 不匹配（答对 hard items 但答错 easy items）。STEM 相对正常 因为 STEM 训练数据覆盖更广。ctrl-contam (QLoRA) 注入的 items 按 random 15% 采样，因此 domain 分布预期 uniform——验证实验设计的内部一致性。 Domain-level 分析的附加价值：为 future auditors 提供 \\\"contamination fingerprinting\\\" 工具——selective domain contamination 暗示 targeted training。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ConStat Comparison (Retest-Based)\",\n    \"description\": \"ConStat (NeurIPS 2024) retest-based comparison on ctrl-contam models。 Part of baseline comparison but requiring additional inference runs。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"constat_retest_auroc\": 0.78,\n      \"constat_n_retests\": 3,\n      \"constat_gpu_hours\": 8,\n      \"constat_vs_lz_star_at_model_level\": \"comparable detection\",\n      \"constat_information_cost\": \"3× inference budget\",\n      \"constat_specificity\": \"higher than acc z-score\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Integrated into baseline comparison table。ConStat 结果强化 detection frontier 叙事——更多信息确实有帮助但 marginal gain 不大。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 ConStat 在 model-level 检测上 AUROC=0.78——有效但不如 lz* 的 d=3.4 直接。ConStat 的 retest 设计需要 rephrased items 和多次推理， 本质上是用\\\"更多信息\\\"换取\\\"更确定的判断\\\"。AUROC 0.78 而非更高是因为： (1) QLoRA SFT 的 memorization 是 partial (~35%)——rephrased items 的 response 变化不如 verbatim 记忆那么 dramatic；(2) SFT 泛化效应使得部分 seen items 即使 rephrased 也答对——这降低了 retest 的 sensitivity。 关键对比：lz* 用 zero 额外推理达到 comparable 检测力——这是 minimal-information operating point 的核心价值。ConStat 在 detection frontier 上位于 \\\"binary + retest\\\" 层级，高于 lz* 的 \\\"binary only\\\" 但低于 \\\"token probs\\\" 层级。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MIA/Min-K++ on SFT Contamination\",\n    \"description\": \"Min-K%++ 和 MIA-loss 在 SFT-contaminated 模型上的表现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mink_sft_auroc\": 0.61,\n      \"mia_loss_sft_auroc\": 0.59,\n      \"mink_base_auroc\": 0.49,\n      \"mia_loss_base_auroc\": 0.49,\n      \"mink_post_rl_auroc\": 0.51,\n      \"interpretation\": \"SFT produces weak token-level signal, RL washes it\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Token-Level Methods Across Training Stages\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"base_auroc\",\n          \"sft_auroc\",\n          \"post_rl_auroc\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            0.49,\n            0.61,\n            0.51\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MIA-loss\",\n            0.49,\n            0.59,\n            0.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PPL-based\",\n            0.5,\n            0.56,\n            0.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Confirms binary-only person-fit is NOT inferior to token-prob methods for SFT contamination。Token methods' weakness validates the minimal-information framing——more information (token probs) doesn't necessarily help when the contamination mechanism is SFT-style.\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 Min-K%++ 在 SFT contamination 上 AUROC=0.61——高于 random 但远低于 lz* 的 model-level detection (d=3.4)。SFT 确实在 token-level 留下微弱信号（seen items 的 perplexity 略低），但 QLoRA 的 low-rank constraint 限制了 memorization 精度——模型学到的是 \\\"pattern-level\\\" 而非 \\\"token-level\\\" 的记忆，导致 Min-K%++ 这种依赖 token-level anomaly 的 方法效果有限。这与 MIA-loss 类似 (AUROC=0.59)——两者本质上测量同一信号 (token probability anomaly) 的不同 summary。Base model (未 SFT) 上两者 ~random (0.49) 因为没有 memorization 信号。Post-RL 时 AUROC 回到 ~0.51 (near random)——RL 的 distributional shift 完全掩盖了残余的 token-level signal，与 Wang et al. (2025) 一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ARC-C Benchmark Validation (Small Benchmark)\",\n    \"description\": \"ARC-Challenge (295 items) 上的控制实验——验证 small benchmark 检测极限。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"arcc_clean_lz\": -5.5,\n      \"arcc_contam15_lz\": -4.9,\n      \"arcc_contam50_lz\": -4.6,\n      \"arcc_delta_lz_15\": 0.6,\n      \"arcc_delta_lz_50\": 0.9,\n      \"arcc_cohens_d_15_free\": -0.5,\n      \"arcc_cohens_d_50_free\": -0.8,\n      \"arcc_theta_fixed_d_15\": 0.8,\n      \"arcc_theta_fixed_d_50\": 1.2,\n      \"arcc_power_theory_15\": 0.129,\n      \"arcc_memo_frac\": 0.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: ARC-C Detection (Small Benchmark Regime)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"delta_lz\",\n          \"d_free\",\n          \"d_theta_fixed\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"clean (mean)\",\n            -5.5,\n            0,\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_15\",\n            -4.9,\n            0.6,\n            -0.5,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_50\",\n            -4.6,\n            0.9,\n            -0.8,\n            1.2\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ARC-C 结果验证 power theory 预测——小 benchmark 检测力弱是理论预期。 θ-fixed 部分补偿但不改变根本限制。论文中作为 Claim 2 的支撑证据—— detection power 与 n_items 的关系在实际数据中得到验证。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预期 ARC-C (295 items) 在 free-θ 下检测力很弱 (d ~0.5 at 15%) 因为 power theory 预测仅 12.9% power。295 items 的 lz* 方差大——noise floor 高导致 signal/noise ratio 低。θ-fixed 改善至 d ~0.8-1.2 因为消除了 θ-shift confound，但仍远低于 MMLU 的 d=3.4。Memorization fraction ~30% 意味着 15% contamination 仅 ~44 items 被记忆——在 295 items 中产生的 pattern distortion 不够大。这与 power theory 的 min_items_15pct_80power =7958 一致——ARC-C 远低于此阈值。θ-fixed analysis 的 arcc_theta_fixed_d 在 [0.5, 1.5] 范围内——detectable 但效应弱。这是一个\\\"honest characterization\\\" 而非限制——小 benchmark 的检测力弱是信息论预期。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"HT vs lz* Post-RL Differentiation\",\n    \"description\": \"Post-RL 条件下 HT 与 lz* 的 differential robustness 测试。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lz_star_post_rl_d\": 1.5,\n      \"ht_post_rl_d\": 1.3,\n      \"lz_star_ht_ratio_post_rl\": 1.15,\n      \"lz_star_ht_ratio_pre_rl\": 1.07,\n      \"differentiation_significant\": false,\n      \"differentiation_p_value\": 0.35\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: lz* vs HT Post-RL Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"statistic\",\n          \"pre_rl_d\",\n          \"post_rl_d\",\n          \"retention\",\n          \"ratio_lz_over_ht\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz*\",\n            -3.42,\n            -1.5,\n            \"44%\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HT\",\n            -3.21,\n            -1.3,\n            \"40%\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ratio\",\n            1.07,\n            1.15,\n            \"-\",\n            \"n.s. (p=0.35)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档叙事应对（对应 R12 reviewer concern）：empirical differentiation 失败 → 激活数据无关差异化三论证：(i) parametric null N(0,1)——bootstrap 已验证 lz* null 分布 mean=0.09/std=1.00，HT 无此性质，需 per-case bootstrap； (ii) Snijders correction Var*=Var_l - C²/I(θ) 补偿 θ 估计误差——尤其在 θ-fixed 不可用时 (e.g., retrospective audit without clean baseline)； (iii) 4PL a-weighting 在 MMLU 57 subjects 高异质性下理论更精确——虽然 empirical d 差异不显著，但信息论上 lz* 使用了更多 item-level information。 论文应坦诚报告并将这些论证置于 Discussion §6。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心预期：lz* 和 HT post-RL 退化幅度相似，差异不显著 (p=0.35)。 ratio 从 pre-RL 1.07 微升至 1.15——lz* 略好但 n=1 (单一模型) 条件下无法 得出统计结论。原因：post-RL 的 signal degradation 作用于 response pattern level——RL 改变了模型对 items 的作答方式（从记忆转向推理），这一变化对所有 基于 response pattern 的统计量影响相似。lz* 的 4PL weighting 在 large n (14K items) 下的优势被 RL-induced noise 部分抵消。HT 的 robustness 来自其 simplicity——仅依赖 difficulty ordering，RL 对 difficulty ordering 的扰动 较小。结论：无法通过 post-RL 实验 empirically differentiate lz* vs HT—— 转用数据无关差异化策略。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Mistral n=1 Supporting Evidence\",\n    \"description\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 单 clean seed 控制实验——作为第三个 family 的 supporting evidence。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mistral_clean_lz\": 5.42,\n      \"mistral_contam15_lz\": -1.38,\n      \"mistral_contam50_lz\": -3.15,\n      \"mistral_delta_lz_15\": -6.8,\n      \"mistral_delta_lz_50\": -8.57,\n      \"mistral_acc_clean\": 0.514,\n      \"mistral_contam15_acc\": 0.595,\n      \"mistral_memo_frac_15\": 0.34,\n      \"mistral_n_clean_seeds\": 1,\n      \"mistral_cohens_d_estimate\": \"N/A (n=1, no variance estimate)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Mistral Supporting Evidence (n=1)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"delta_lz\",\n          \"acc\",\n          \"theta\",\n          \"memo_frac\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            5.42,\n            0,\n            0.514,\n            -1.157,\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_15\",\n            -1.38,\n            -6.8,\n            0.595,\n            -0.713,\n            0.34\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_50\",\n            -3.15,\n            -8.57,\n            0.673,\n            -0.303,\n            0.29\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Supporting evidence。n=1 不支持独立 claim 但与 Qwen/Llama 一致的方向性 结果增强跨家族泛化叙事。注意 Mistral 的 Δlz* 绝对值更大反映的是低能力 模型的更强 contamination signal——与 power theory 一致（低 θ baseline → 更大 response pattern shift）。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档 Mistral 仅 n=1 clean seed——无法计算 Cohen's d 或 CI。但 Δlz*=-6.80 (15%) 的绝对值比 Qwen (-4.84) 和 Llama (-2.85) 更大，因为 Mistral 是最弱模型 (acc=0.514)——低能力模型受 contamination 的 response pattern distortion 更大（baseline 答错很多 items，contamination 后这些 items 突然答对，产生更极端的 aberrance）。Mistral baseline lz*=5.42 (正值) 意味着 clean model 已经 slightly over-consistent——contamination 后 lz* 翻转至负值 (-1.38) 说明 aberrance signal 足够强。作为 n=1 supporting evidence 而非 primary validation——论文中明确标注 \\\"single-seed, indicative\\\"。跨三个 family (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 的 detection success 足以支撑 n_families_validated=3。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Baseline Comparison Table (Frontier Ranking)\",\n    \"description\": \"Detection frontier 完整排名表——所有方法按信息访问层级排列。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_baselines_total\": 7,\n      \"n_baselines_beaten_at_model_level\": 4,\n      \"frontier_ranking\": {\n        \"binary_only\": [\n          \"Guttman (d=0.43)\",\n          \"U3 (d=0.38)\",\n          \"random (d=0)\"\n        ],\n        \"binary_plus_difficulty\": [\n          \"HT (d=3.21)\"\n        ],\n        \"binary_plus_4pl\": [\n          \"lz* (d=3.42)\"\n        ],\n        \"binary_plus_retest\": [\n          \"ConStat (AUROC=0.78)\"\n        ],\n        \"token_probs\": [\n          \"Min-K%++ (AUROC=0.61)\",\n          \"MIA-loss (AUROC=0.59)\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"key_comparison\": \"person-fit family (HT + lz*) >> pure binary (Guttman/U3) >> token-prob (Min-K++)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Detection Frontier Ranking\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"info_access\",\n          \"model_d_or_auroc\",\n          \"item_auroc\",\n          \"extra_cost\",\n          \"interpretable\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz* (ours)\",\n            \"binary + 4PL params\",\n            \"d=-3.42\",\n            0.536,\n            \"0 (calibrated params available)\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HT\",\n            \"binary + difficulty\",\n            \"d=-3.21\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            0,\n            \"Limited\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"acc z-score\",\n            \"binary + pop stats\",\n            \"z=160.6\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            0,\n            \"No (no specificity)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            \"binary + retest\",\n            \"AUROC=0.78\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            \"3× inference\",\n            \"Partial\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            \"token probs\",\n            \"AUROC=0.61\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            \"API access\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MIA-loss\",\n            \"token probs\",\n            \"AUROC=0.59\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            \"API access\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Guttman/U3\",\n            \"binary only\",\n            \"d=-0.43\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            0,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random\",\n            \"none\",\n            \"d=0\",\n            0.5,\n            0,\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT tied。ConStat effective but higher info cost。Acc z-score 不 comparable (no specificity)。 Total ≥5 baselines 满足同行中位数要求。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档 frontier ranking 清晰呈现信息层级与检测力的关系：(1) 纯 binary (Guttman/U3) 最弱因为不利用 item difficulty 信息——仅看 response pattern 的 non-randomness，无法区分 high-ability 与 contamination；(2) binary + difficulty (HT) 跳跃式提升至 d=3.21——difficulty ordering 是关键信息， 让统计量能识别 \\\"答对不该答对的题\\\"；(3) binary + 4PL (lz*) 在 HT 基础上 marginal gain——a/c/d 参数的额外信息在 14K items 下被 averaging 稀释； (4) token-prob methods 反而弱于 binary person-fit——说明 \\\"更多信息\\\" 不等于 \\\"更好检测\\\"，信息类型比信息量重要。SFT contamination 的 token-level signal 很弱 (memorization fraction ~35%)，而 response-pattern-level signal 通过 14K items 聚合后很强。这是论文的核心 insight 之一。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Gemma-4-31B Controlled Contamination (Conditional)\",\n    \"description\": \"Gemma-4-31B 控制实验——第四个 family，median 档下可能部分失败。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gemma_training_stable\": \"uncertain\",\n      \"gemma_qlora_rank\": 64,\n      \"gemma_gpu_hours\": 20,\n      \"gemma_clean_lz\": 3.2,\n      \"gemma_contam15_d\": -2.2,\n      \"gemma_contam50_d\": -2.8,\n      \"gemma_partial_failure_risk\": 0.35,\n      \"gemma_memo_frac\": 0.32,\n      \"fallback\": \"drop to 3 families if training unstable\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Gemma Conditional Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"delta_lz\",\n          \"d_estimate\",\n          \"training_status\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            3.2,\n            0,\n            \"-\",\n            \"stable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_15\",\n            \"~0.5\",\n            \"-2.7\",\n            -2.2,\n            \"stable/unstable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_50\",\n            \"~-0.8\",\n            \"-4.0\",\n            -2.8,\n            \"stable/unstable\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Conditional on training stability。如果成功 → n_families_validated=4 (bonus)。如果失败 → 3 families 已足够，Gemma 的 scale difference (31B vs 7-9B) 写入 Limitations 作为 future work。\\n\\nMedian 档 Gemma-4-31B 是最不确定的实验。31B 参数量显著大于其他三个 (7-9B)， QLoRA 行为可能不同：(1) rank=64 的 low-rank adaptation 在 31B 模型上 adaptation 比例更小——可能需要更多 epochs 或更高 rank；(2) Gemma 架构 (Google) 与 Qwen/Llama/Mistral 不同——可能有不同的 SFT 泛化特性； (3) 训练不稳定风险 ~35%（loss divergence or poor convergence）。如果成功， d ~2.2-2.8 处于可接受范围。如果部分失败（如某些 contamination levels 不收敛）， 降级为 footnote evidence。3 families (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 已足够支撑 cross-family claim——Gemma 是 bonus。Memorization fraction 可能略低 (0.32) 因为大模型 QLoRA 的 effective capacity 更分散。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1221,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1221}}}
